var scenariolist = [
["Tutorial Scenarios"],
["tutorial.xml", "Tutorial — Khalkhin Gol", "Tutorial — Khalkhin Gol<br>3 July 1939<br>Japanese forces have crossed the Khalkhin Gol and occupied positions around the Bain-Tsagan heights. The first three turns are an AI-controlled demonstration of objectives, unit information, transport, reconnaissance, artillery preparation, support fire, reinforcement, resupply, and OverRun. At the start of turn 4, full control of the Soviet-Mongolian detachment passes to you. Capture the Khaylastyn Crossing and the Hamar-Daba Command Post; the Bain-Tsagan Observation Point is optional.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [20, 24]}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["Red Army Campaign (1936-1945)"],
["bn9s00.xml", "Battle of Sesena", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. BATTLE OF SESENA - 29 OCT 1936 places your command at South of Madrid, Spain. South of Madrid, Spain Comrade, here is your order - Move west with your armored forces and occupy the towns of Esquivias and Illescas! Support this move with your air force. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF LAKE KHASAN - 2 AUG 1938. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 28}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [26]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s01.xml", "Battle of Lake Khasan", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. BATTLE OF LAKE KHASAN - 2 AUG 1938 places your command at Lake Khasan, Far East of Soviet Union. Lake Khasan, Far East of Soviet Union The sneaky Japanese attacked and beaten our border troops on the Bezymyannaya and Zaozyornaya hills. Attack the Japanese with superior power and recapture the territories we deserve! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to KHALKHIN GOL - 3 JUL 1939. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s02.xml", "Khalkhin Gol", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. KHALKHIN GOL - 3 JUL 1939 places your command at Khalkhin Gol River, Mongolian People's Republic. Khalkhin Gol River, Mongolian People's Republic The Japanese crossed the Khalkhin Gol river in the north, occupied the Baintsagan hills and tried to surround our troops with a two-pronged assault. Carry out a vigorous counterattack, thwart the enemy intentions and occupy the Japanese positions west and east of the river! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [23]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s03.xml", "Battle of Grodno", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. BATTLE OF GRODNO - 20 SEP 1939 places your command at Southeast of Grodno, East Poland. Southeast of Grodno, East Poland Move your units across the city of Grodno to the Lithuanian border. Occupy the city and vicinity and break any resistance! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to RAATE ROAD - 2 JAN 1940. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [60]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s04.xml", "Raate Road", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. RAATE ROAD - 2 JAN 1940 places your command at Raate-Suomussalmi Road, Eastern Finland. Raate-Suomussalmi Road, Eastern Finland Our comrades from the 163rd division in Suomussalmi are cut off and need help. Break through the enemy encirclement and restore the supply route! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to VYBORG BAY - 5 MAR 1940. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s05.xml", "Vyborg Bay", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. VYBORG BAY - 5 MAR 1940 places your command at Karelian Isthmus, Finland. Karelian Isthmus, Finland The Finns asked for a ceasefire because their front is collapsing. But before peace comes, we have to capture the west bank of Vyborg Bay and the city itself! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF BIALYSTOK-MINSK - 27 JUN 1941. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s06.xml", "Battle of Bialystok-Minsk", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. BATTLE OF BIALYSTOK-MINSK - 27 JUN 1941 places your command at West of Minsk, Belarus. West of Minsk, Belarus The treacherous Germans have launched a general attack on our homeland. The western front has collapsed and most of our troops are threatened to be encircled west of Minsk. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to YELNYA OFFENSIVE - 2 SEP 1941. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}, {"id": 2, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s07.xml", "Yelnya Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. YELNYA OFFENSIVE - 2 SEP 1941 places your command at Yelnya, Southeast of Smolensk. Yelnya, Southeast of Smolensk You'll lead the attack against the semi-circular Yelnya salient which the Germans had extended 50 kilometres south-east of Smolensk, forming a staging area for an offensive towards Vyazma and eventually Moscow. Eliminate the threat and win the much-needed victory for us, Comrade! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF MOSCOW - 9 DEC 1941. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s08.xml", "Battle of Moscow", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. BATTLE OF MOSCOW - 9 DEC 1941 places your command at Dmitrow, North of Moscow. Dmitrow, North of Moscow The German offensives against our capital were halted and our strategic counter-offensive started. Your goal is to cross the Moscow-Leningrad railway line and to liberate the city of Klin. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to SECOND BATTLE OF KHARKOV - 12 MAY 1942. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s09.xml", "Second Battle of Kharkov", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. SECOND BATTLE OF KHARKOV - 12 MAY 1942 places your command at Volchansk, Northeast of Kharkov. Volchansk, Northeast of Kharkov We'll start an offensive to liberate Kharkov. With a dual pincer movement from the Volchansk and Barvenkovo salients, we'll surround and free the city. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF VORONEZH - 28 JUN 1942. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 37, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s10.xml", "Battle of Voronezh", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. BATTLE OF VORONEZH - 28 JUN 1942 places your command at Volovo, Northwest of Voronezh. Volovo, Northwest of Voronezh The Germans launch an offensive towards Voronezh. Strong forces are trying to break through our defensive positions. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to TATSINSKAYA RAID - 22 DEC 1942. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 41]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s11.xml", "Tatsinskaya Raid", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. TATSINSKAYA RAID - 22 DEC 1942 places your command at Bol'shinka, 200km west of Stalingrad. Bol'shinka, 200km west of Stalingrad You'll lead a raid deep into the German rear - the target is the enemy airfield at Tatsinskaya, the primary operating base for the German airlift efforts to Stalingrad. Inflict significant losses on enemy Air Force by destroying as many planes as possible and force the Germans to divert forces attempting to relieve their forces encircled in Stalingrad! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s12.xml", "Third Battle of Kharkov", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. THIRD BATTLE OF KHARKOV - 7 MAR 1943 places your command at South of Kharkov, Ukraine. South of Kharkov, Ukraine We expect a German attack on Kharkov again. Stop the attack and inflict maximum losses on the enemy! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF KURSK - 11 JUL 1943. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s13.xml", "Battle of Kursk", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. BATTLE OF KURSK - 11 JUL 1943 places your command at South of Kursk, Russia. South of Kursk, Russia Despite our prepared defensive positions the Germans continue their advance on Kursk. You will counterattack at Prokhorovka and throw back the Germans before they break through the last lines of defense towards Kursk. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to ZHITOMIR-BERDICHEV OFFENSIVE - 27 DEC 1943. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s14.xml", "Zhitomir-Berdichev Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. ZHITOMIR-BERDICHEV OFFENSIVE - 27 DEC 1943 places your command at East of Zhitomir, Ukraine. East of Zhitomir, Ukraine You task is to defeat the opposing German 4th Panzer Army of Army Group South and the liberation of the Zhytomyr Oblast region, including the cities of Zhitomir and Berdichev. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to CRIMEAN OFFENSIVE - 7 MAY 1944. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [17, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [47]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s15.xml", "Crimean Offensive", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. CRIMEAN OFFENSIVE - 7 MAY 1944 places your command at East of Sevastopol, Crimea peninsula. East of Sevastopol, Crimea peninsula You're honored to liberate our beloved Sevastopol. The Germans and Romanians have already started evacuation by sea. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to JASSY-KISHINEV OFFENSIVE - 20 AUG 1944. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s16.xml", "Jassy-Kishinev Offensive", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. JASSY-KISHINEV OFFENSIVE - 20 AUG 1944 places your command at North of Jassy, Eastern Romania. North of Jassy, Eastern Romania In our major offensive on Romania you and your troops will be deployed on the right wing of the attack front. The goal is to encircle and destroy the enemy's 6th Army. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to BELGRADE OFFENSIVE - 12 OCT 1944. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s17.xml", "Belgrade Offensive", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. BELGRADE OFFENSIVE - 12 OCT 1944 places your command at West of Belgrade, Serbia. West of Belgrade, Serbia The time has come to liberate the Serbian capital from the fascist bondage! With the support of the Yugoslav Partisans and the Bulgarian Army, it should not be difficult to drive out the Germans and their collaborators. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to LAKE BALATON COUNTERATTACK - 16 MAR 1945. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}, {"id": 2, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s18.xml", "Lake Balaton Counterattack", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. LAKE BALATON COUNTERATTACK - 16 MAR 1945 places your command at East of Lake Balaton, Hungary. East of Lake Balaton, Hungary The German offensive flagged - the enemy isn't be able to break through to the Danube. Advance to Lake Balaton and crush the enemy formations! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to ROAD TO VIENNA - 3 APR 1945. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s19.xml", "Road to Vienna", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. ROAD TO VIENNA - 3 APR 1945 places your command at East of Vienna, Austria. East of Vienna, Austria The Germans are on the run - withdrawing towards Vienna. Chase the enemy and destroy as many units as possible so that the enemy cannot establish an effective line of defense in front of Vienna! The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. A strong result opens the road to MANCHURIAN OFFENSIVE - 9 AUG 1945. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s20.xml", "Manchurian Offensive", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. MANCHURIAN OFFENSIVE - 9 AUG 1945 places your command at Khabarovsk, Far Eastern Russia. Khabarovsk, Far Eastern Russia At the Tehran and Yalta Conference, the Soviet Union has promised to enter the Pacific Theater within three months after the end of the war in Europe. So we are going to smash the Japanese puppet state of Manchukuo with a powerful operation. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY You have achieved most objectives comrade, the operation was a success. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Stay Alive - Red Partisans (1941-1945)"],
["bn5s01.xml", "RP Guerrilla Hunter", "A smaller force can still dictate the battle when it chooses where the battle begins. GUERRILLA HUNTER - 2 JUL 1941 places your command at HQ 8th NKVD Rife Brigade, Estonia. HQ 8th NKVD Rife Brigade, Estonia CO General Kuznetsov It does not look good for us, Comrade! The Germans stand at the Estonian border and all over crawled Bandits out of their holes. The wider stakes are clear: A serious defeat for the Estonian bandits and their Finnish friends. A strong result opens the road to BLITZ - 10 JUL 1941. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 58}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn5s02.xml", "RP German Blitz", "There is no continuous front here—only terrain, secrecy, and the moment chosen for the first shot. BLITZ - 10 JUL 1941 places your command at HQ 8th NKVD Rife Brigade, Estonia. HQ 8th NKVD Rife Brigade, Estonia CO General Kuznetsov The Nazi war machine stand at our gates, Comrade! And your fate is the defense of Dorpat. The wider stakes are clear: Go with your remains into the forests and form a partisan group to fight against the Fascists from behind! A strong result opens the road to SINK THE TIRPITZ - 5 OCT 1941. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s09.xml", "RP Sink the Tirpitz", "Strike hard, disappear quickly, and leave the occupier afraid of every path and village. SINK THE TIRPITZ - 5 OCT 1941 places your command at HQ Soviet Partisans, Estonia. HQ Soviet Partisans, Estonia CO General Karotamm The largest German battleship, the Tirpitz, flagship of a fleet, which has supported the German landings on the Baltic islands, anchored off the coast and poses a serious threat for our Baltic fleet. Maritime forces are not available that could match with this ship. The wider stakes are clear: General Karotamm A great success that make headlines. A strong result opens the road to HIT & RUN - 28 APR 1942. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s03.xml", "RP Hit & Run", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. HIT & RUN - 28 APR 1942 places your command at HQ Soviet Partisans, Lithuania. HQ Soviet Partisans, Lithuania CO General Karotamm Comrade, its time to strike the invaders where it hurts. You'll attack a weak defended German supply depot and raise the Red Banner on its ruins! The wider stakes are clear: General Karotamm Your attack was a success, the depot was badly damaged! A strong result opens the road to REVENGE - 8 OCT 1942. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [60]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s08.xml", "RP Revenge", "Strike hard, disappear quickly, and leave the occupier afraid of every path and village. REVENGE - 8 OCT 1942 places your command at HQ Soviet Partisans, Latvia. HQ Soviet Partisans, Latvia CO General Karotamm Parts of an SS-Division were moved in our area for rest and refreshing. It is a unit well-known as Anti-Partisan combat formation and has spread terror among the Soviet population. The wider stakes are clear: General Karotamm The leadership of the SS division is destroyed. A strong result opens the road to OPERATION GYBSY BARON - 15 JUN 1943. Avoid a fair fight, strike communications and isolated units, and withdraw before superior firepower can be brought to bear.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [59, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s06.xml", "RP Gypsy Baron", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. OPERATION GYBSY BARON - 15 JUN 1943 places your command at HQ Soviet Partisans, Belarus. HQ Soviet Partisans, Belarus CO General Karotamm That we have interrupted the supply routes for their offensive at Kursk, has not pleased the Germans. They'll try to force us out of this area. The wider stakes are clear: General Karotamm The Germans sent criminal traitors in the battle. A strong result opens the road to RESCUE MISSION - 12 SEP 1943. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 1, "country": 359, "support": [7, 59]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s04.xml", "RP Rescue Mission", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. RESCUE MISSION - 12 SEP 1943 places your command at HQ Soviet Partisans, Estonia. HQ Soviet Partisans, Estonia CO General Karotamm A plane loaded with a important U.S. politician, on his way to Moscow, was forced to make an emergency landing in our area. A British submarine, ready to take our guest is waiting off the coast. The wider stakes are clear: Moscow is very pleased with the outcome of this mission! A strong result opens the road to KILL BRUNO - 28 JAN 1944. Avoid a fair fight, strike communications and isolated units, and withdraw before superior firepower can be brought to bear.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [9, 22, 361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s07.xml", "RP Kill Bruno", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. KILL BRUNO - 28 JAN 1944 places your command at HQ Soviet Partisans, Estonia. The Germans consider their rail gun safe, because any direct attack is smashed by the Luftwaffe. The eastern airfield is to seize with your troops. The wider stakes are clear: General Karotamm The Rail gun is destroyed, excellent work. A strong result opens the road to NARVA - 24 JUL 1944. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn5s05.xml", "RP Narva", "Strike hard, disappear quickly, and leave the occupier afraid of every path and village. NARVA - 24 JUL 1944 places your command at HQ 2nd Shock Army. HQ 2nd Shock Army CO General Fedyuninsky Comrade, we want to break the German defense at Narva in an all out attack. Our objective is to seize Narva, break through the Tannenberg Line, and occupy all enemy ports, airfields, and key cities. The wider stakes are clear: General Fedyuninsky The Germans are defeated, the way to Tallinn is open! A strong result opens the road to AUGUST STORM - 12 AUG 1945. Avoid a fair fight, strike communications and isolated units, and withdraw before superior firepower can be brought to bear.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [17, 35, 40]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s10.xml", "RP August Storm", "There is no continuous front here—only terrain, secrecy, and the moment chosen for the first shot. AUGUST STORM - 12 AUG 1945 places your command at HQ Transbaikal Front, Manchuria. HQ Transbaikal Front, Manchuria CO General Malinovsky Comrade, the liberation of Manchuria from Japanese occupation making good progress on all fronts. Outstanding work, but now the heavily defended area around Solon is our next target. The wider stakes are clear: General Malinovsky The Japanese will surrender soon and we dictate the terms! Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Yugoslav Front (1941-1945)"],
["bn8s00.xml", "Uprising in Serbia", "There is no continuous front here—only terrain, secrecy, and the moment chosen for the first shot. UPRISING IN SERBIA - 25 Aug 1941 places your command at North of Bela Crkva, Macva Region, Serbia. You will lead the attack to liberate the provincial capital Krupanj! But first we need the arms depots of the Gendarmerie in the surrounding villages and as many men as possible before we can dare to attack. The wider stakes are clear: BACKGROUND The Uprising in Yugoslavia was initiated in July 1941 by the Communist Party of Yugoslavia against the German occupation forces and their Serbian quisling auxiliaries in the Territory of the Military Commander in Serbia. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [66]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s01.xml", "Battle of Sabac", "There is no continuous front here—only terrain, secrecy, and the moment chosen for the first shot. BATTLE OF SABAC - 18 Sep 1941 places your command at North of Sabac, Macva Region, Serbia. North of Sabac, Macva Region, Serbia CO Commander Nebojsa Jerkovic We will take advantage of our success of the last weeks and extend the free territories fast. You will perform a attack against the strong German garrison of Sabac and free the city from fascism. The wider stakes are clear: In mid-September 1941, Josip Broz Tito and the Partisan General Staff moved from Belgrade to the Uzice Republic where the Partisans had by now formed 25 new military detachments. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [66]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s02.xml", "Betrayal", "There is no continuous front here—only terrain, secrecy, and the moment chosen for the first shot. BETRAYAL - 1 Nov 1941 places your command at East of Uzice, Zlatibor Region, Serbia. East of Uzice, Zlatibor Region, Serbia CO Commander Koca Popovic We have information about an imminent attack of the treacherous Chetniks on our headquarters in Uzice. March with your comrades as soon as possible to Uzice and beat back the attackers! The wider stakes are clear: Tito and Mihailovic met again on October 26 or 27, 1941 in the town of Brajici near Ravna Gora in a final attempt to achieve an understanding, but found consensus only on secondary issues. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 66}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn8s03.xml", "Retreat to Montenegro", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. RETREAT TO MONTENEGRO - 2 Dec 1941 places your command at Southwest of Nova Varos, Zlatibor Region, Serbia. Southwest of Nova Varos, Zlatibor Region, Serbia CO Commander Koca Popovic After a surprisingly strong German counterattack, our positions in Serbia have become untenable. Lead your comrades over the Lim River and cross the border at Dobrakovo. The wider stakes are clear: At the end of 1941, there were six Partisan detachments in eastern Bosnia, with about 7,300 fighters operating in the Majevica, Ozren, Birac, Romanija, Zvijezda and Kalinovik areas. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 12]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s04.xml", "Rail Raid", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. RAIL RAID - 8 Feb 1942 places your command at Railway between Mostar and Sarajevo, Bosnia. Railway between Mostar and Sarajevo, Bosnia CO Commander Koca Popovic Some German armored trains are on their way from Mostar to Belgrade. Then it should be possible to destroy these trains by a concentrated attack of your forces. The wider stakes are clear: You have achieved all objectives, the mission was a complete success. A strong result opens the road to OPERATION TRIO - 10 May 1942. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s05.xml", "Operation Trio", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. OPERATION TRIO - 10 May 1942 places your command at Foca, Srpska Region, Bosnia. Foca, Srpska Region, Bosnia CO Commander Koca Popovic Italians, Croats and Chetniks have launched a large-scale operation against our liberated territory. Cover the retreat of the 1st Proletarian Brigade, especially the Brigade HQ! The wider stakes are clear: Within a few weeks of the end of Operation Trio only 600 Partisan fighters were left in eastern Bosnia, comprising the Group of Shock Battalions and the Birac Partisan Detachment. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [12, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s06.xml", "Counterattack on Kljuc", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. COUNTERATTACK ON KLIJUC - 7 Oct 1942 places your command at West of Kljuc, Una-Sana Region, Bosnia. West of Kljuc, Una-Sana Region, Bosnia CO Commander Koca Popovic Few days ago the fascists managed to capture the city Kljuc. Attack Kljuc, liberate the city and cut off the withdrawal Fascists and destroy them! The wider stakes are clear: You have achieved all objectives, the mission was a complete success. A strong result opens the road to CASE WHITE - 30 Feb 1943. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s07.xml", "Case White", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. CASE WHITE - 30 Feb 1943 places your command at Vicinity of the Neretva River, Herzegovina. We must retreat as quickly as possible to Montenegro and our only remaining option is to reach and cross the Neretva River. When air reconnaissance brought this information to the German command, they concluded that the Partisans must be preparing a final dash north of their current position (along the western shore of the Neretva), and had blown up the bridge to prevent desertion as well as attack by Chetnik forces from the other side of the river.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 12, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s08.xml", "Case Black", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. CASE BLACK - 4 Jun 1943 places your command at Vicinity of the Sutjeska River, Southeastern Bosnia. Strong enemy forces have encircled us and try to block our way into eastern Bosnia. The Axis troops used the advantage of better starting positions to encircle and isolate the partisans on the Durmitor mountain area, located between the Tara and Piva rivers in the mountainous areas of northern Montenegro and forced them to engage in a fierce month-long battle on waste territory. The wider stakes are clear: The operation immediately followed Case White which had failed in accomplishing the same objectives: to eliminate the central Partisan formations and capture their commander, Marshal Josip Broz Tito.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 8, 12]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s09.xml", "Operation Istria", "Strike hard, disappear quickly, and leave the occupier afraid of every path and village. OPERATION ISTRIA - 25 Sep 1943 places your command at Vicinity of Petrinja, Central Croatia. Unfortunately the fascists has occupied the most important cities such as Trieste, Rijeka and Zadar before we could intervene. Capture all VH and hold it for 15 turns! The wider stakes are clear: You have achieved all objectives, the mission was a complete success. A strong result opens the road to BANJA LUKA STRIKE - 18 Dec 1943. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [62]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s10.xml", "Banja Luka Strike", "Strike hard, disappear quickly, and leave the occupier afraid of every path and village. BANJA LUKA STRIKE - 18 Dec 1943 places your command at North of Banja Luka, Bosnia. North of Banja Luka, Bosnia CO Commander Slavko Rodic Your Corps will start a surprise attack on the largest town in the region of Srpska. Liberate the citizens of Banja Luka from the fascist bondage! The wider stakes are clear: You have achieved all objectives, the mission was a complete success. A strong result opens the road to KNIGHT'S MOVE - 25 May 1944. Avoid a fair fight, strike communications and isolated units, and withdraw before superior firepower can be brought to bear.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s11.xml", "Knight's Move", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. KNIGHT'S MOVE - 25 May 1944 places your command at Drvar Region, Western Bosnia. Airborne assault and initial response 500th SS Parachute Battalion began to parachute and glide onto their objectives at 7am, with most parachutists and glider pilots able to land relatively close to their targets despite the smoke and dust from the bombing. They split into two groups, a smaller group which crossed the Unac and advanced west along the railway line on the ridge leading toward Tito's cave, and a larger group which collected arms and ammunition from several stray canisters of German equipment dropped by parachute.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [41]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [9, 19, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s12.xml", "Operation Ratweek", "There is no continuous front here—only terrain, secrecy, and the moment chosen for the first shot. OPERATION RATWEEK - 3 Sep 1944 places your command at West of Zagreb, Croatia. In recent days, the USAAF bombed all enemy airfields in Zagreb east of the Sava River. Your task is the capture and destruction of the remaining enemy airfields west of the Sava River! The wider stakes are clear: Allied air force destroyed 112 locomotives, 243 motorized transports and 413 railway carts, also attacks on the airfields destroyed 94 aircraft crippling Luftwaffe strength in Yugoslavia. A strong result opens the road to BELGRADE OFFENSIVE - 12 Oct 1944. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s13.xml", "Belgrade Offensive", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. BELGRADE OFFENSIVE - 12 Oct 1944 places your command at West of Belgrade, Serbia. West of Belgrade, Serbia CO General Peko Dapcevic The time has come to liberate the Serbian capital from the fascist bondage! The Yugoslavs advanced along the roads in the direction of Belgrade south of the Sava River, while the Red Army engaged in fighting on the northern bank outskirts. The wider stakes are clear: The objective was to destroy the forces of the German Army Group E in the Suva Planina region, and those of Army Group F east of Velika Morava river, and ultimately to free Belgrade from Nazi occupation.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [19]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s14.xml", "Knin", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. KNIN - 26 Nov 1944 places your command at South of Knin, Herzegovina. On 28 November Army Group E allowed 15th Mountain Corps to begun retreat from Knin to more defensible position north Knin which were to be held during the winter. On 1 December new assault breaks Germans lines, successful morthen outflanking maneuver by 8th Brigade of the 20th Division attacks German forces in Padene area while 26th Division ties down most of Germans to the southern sector. The wider stakes are clear: BACKGROUND Knin operation in 1944 was launched by Yugoslav Partisans 8th Corps from 7 November to 9 December 1944 with purpose of destroying German, Ustasha and Chetnik formations in the area of Knin.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s15.xml", "Liberation of Mostar", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. LIBERATION OF MOSTAR - 6 Feb 1945 places your command at Sibenik, Croatia. However, the Germans have already started to retreat inland. Advance with a task force as soon as possible on Visoko and with a second along the coast on Dubrovnik. The wider stakes are clear: You have achieved all objectives, the mission was a complete success. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF SARAJEVO - 1 Apr 1945. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s16.xml", "Battle of Sarajevo", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. BATTLE OF SARAJEVO - 1 Apr 1945 places your command at Vicinity of Sarajevo, Bosnia. Vicinity of Sarajevo, Bosnia CO Commander Kosta Nad The encirclement and destruction of the German-Croat forces in the area of Sarajevo is our next planned step. Advance in the rear of the enemy quickly at Podlugovi and cut the Germans off! The wider stakes are clear: You have achieved all objectives, the mission was a complete success. A strong result opens the road to ADVANCE ON TRIESTE - 14 Apr 1945. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 67]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s17.xml", "Advance on Trieste", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. ADVANCE ON TRIESTE - 14 Apr 1945 places your command at Vicinity of Drnis, Croatia. Vicinity of Drnis, Croatia CO Commander Pavle Ilic The last chapter of the liberation of our homeland is opened. Advance with your Corps to Trieste, liberate the city and link up with the from Italy coming Allied troops! The wider stakes are clear: You have achieved all objectives, the mission was a complete success. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF POLJANA - 14 May 1945. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [6, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s18.xml", "Battle of Poljana", "There is no continuous front here—only terrain, secrecy, and the moment chosen for the first shot. BATTLE OF POLJANA - 14 May 1945 places your command at Poljana Region, Slovenia. Poljana Region, Slovenia CO General Kosta Nad Marauding Axis troops, not willing to surrender to us and want to go to British occupied Austria, move toward your positions. Prevent that these units reach the Austrian border. The wider stakes are clear: BACKGROUND The Battle of Poljana (Monday May 14 - Tuesday May 15, 1945) was a battle of World War II in Europe. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [4, 7, 34]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [22, 361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Red Destiny (1946-1954)"],
["rd01.xml", "RD Bialystok Insurrection", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Allow me to brief you on the tactical situation, and the reasons for which you were called here: The citizens of Bialystok are agitating for the return of Polish independence. Unfortunately, it seems that some units of the former Polish Army were able to evade our men during our brief campaign through Poland, and these units have quickly seized the area from our local garrision. The wider stakes are clear: You have taught the Poles that it is dangerous to interfere with the war effort. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd02.xml", "RD Road To Berlin", "A city is not captured in a single blow; it is taken district by district under smoke and fire. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. The final approach to Berlin has begun. The foolish Germans have left the approach through the Seelow Heights minimally guarded by their lightest units. The wider stakes are clear: Berlin lies open to us, and soon we will take the decadent German Reich out of the war. Secure the approaches, protect your supply route, and reduce the enemy's positions one district at a time.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 86}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd03.xml", "RD Siege Of Berlin", "Urban ground compresses the front and magnifies every mistake. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Here lies the German capital of Berlin. You have been selected by party officials to lead the attack. The wider stakes are clear: The Germans have been eliminated from the war, and the road is open to western Europe. Secure the approaches, protect your supply route, and reduce the enemy's positions one district at a time.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 86, "support": [22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd04a.xml", "RD Border Clash At Ulan-Ude", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Due to your exceptional performance in Berlin, the Party has asked you take a transfer to the Far East. Here, China has been ravaged by an internal war for well over a decade. The wider stakes are clear: Your work is not done, though, and we must continue to perservere against the Chinese dogs. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd05a.xml", "RD Liberation In Almaty", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. There has been a perpetual state of warfare along the Kazakh front for the past five months. The decadent Chinese recently launched an attack on the city of Almaty and took it from our brave conscripts. The wider stakes are clear: Your action in Almaty has forced the Chinese armies back and secured an important propaganda victory. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd04b.xml", "RD Beachhead At Taranto", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Have you ever been to Italy? Well, you will soon be taking a, how shall we say, tour of the country, da? The wider stakes are clear: Your success at Taranto has the Allied dogs running in fear of the Red Army. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd05b.xml", "RD Advance On Salerno", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. The fight for Italy still continues, comrade General. However, the party believes the Italian government is on the verge of surrender. The wider stakes are clear: The Italian government has surrendered to the glorious Soviet Union, and in doing so has forcibly expelled all Allied troops from Italian territory. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd04c.xml", "RD Evacuation In Thermopylae", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. The Party has selected you for tactical operations in the invasion of Greece due to your performance in Berlin. I'm sure you know already that the Western nations believe they can hold us off until they can evacuate the country, da? The wider stakes are clear: The only Allied bastion in Greece that remains is the island of Crete. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [11, 39, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd05c.xml", "RD Landing At Maleme", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. The Allies are using the Greek island of Crete as a last bastion. With the Greek government officially out of the picture, this island is the last obstacle to our rightful rule of the Aegean Sea. The wider stakes are clear: Crete is secure, and the Royal Navy lies at the bottom of the sea. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd06.xml", "RD Drive on Antwerp", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Our glorious Red Army of workers and peasants has begun the invasion of the Low Countries. Holland fell quickly to our armored forces, but I am most displeased to inform you that the Allied pigs have managed to set up significant defenses around the Belgian port of Antwerp. The wider stakes are clear: The city of Antwerp now lies under our rightful control, and Belgium will soon fall to our superior armed forces. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd07.xml", "RD Frostbite in the Ardennes", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. The Allies have laid a trap in the Ardennes, and Russia's brave soldiers are now bogged down in a hellish forest. Your job, comrade General, is to lead them out of this pocket into the beautiful French countryside. The wider stakes are clear: Due to this display of your abilities, Comrade Stalin himself has chosen you to lead the drive to the English Channel. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 6, "support": [22, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd08.xml", "RD Push To Dunkirk", "Preserve the army today so that it can fight—and win—tomorrow. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. The Allied cowards think they can escape socialist justice. The pathetic remnants of the French army are attempting to escape at Dunkirk, with assistance from German and British troops. The wider stakes are clear: The French Army is finally and totally defeated, and our forces control the country. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 6, "support": [22, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd09a.xml", "RD Storming Dover '51", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Over a year has passed since the Allies fled Europe from the city of Dunkirk, and now our carefully made plans are going into action. Your decorated forces have been specially chosen by comrade Stalin himself to land on the British mainland and secure the beaches at Dover. The wider stakes are clear: Do not disappoint us in your next battle Comrade General. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd10a.xml", "RD The Sack Of London '52", "Urban ground compresses the front and magnifies every mistake. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. This is the last battle, comrade General! The British capital of London lies before our glorious Red Army of workers and peasants. The wider stakes are clear: The Second Great War A summary of the conflict from 1946-1952 (The following excerpt has been taken from The Second Great War, a definitive summary of the conflict that engulfed the world from 1946-1952. Use artillery and infantry together, isolate strongpoints, and avoid wasting elite units in unsupported assaults.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd09b.xml", "RD Passage To Madrid", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. We have finally rid France of the Allied scum. Unfortunately, the French armies to the south were able to retreat into the mountains of Spain and Andorra, supported by a weak pro-Allied Spanish government. The wider stakes are clear: The Spanish government has collapsed with the seizure of Madrid, and so their monetary support to the Allies has given way as well. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd10b.xml", "RD Fortress at Gibraltar", "Enemy pressure is building faster than reinforcements can arrive. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Here at the port of Gibraltar, the Allied dogs have made their final stand in continental Europe. It is up to you, comrade General, to expel them from their hiding spot. The wider stakes are clear: Though you took Gibraltar and removed the last Allied bastion in continental Europe, you have done so at great cost in lives and material, causing humiliation for the Soviet Union. The objective is not merely to endure, but to hold enough strength for the counterstroke that follows.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd11.xml", "RD Kharkov Rebellion", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Despite our recent successes in driving the Allies out of Europe, the Ukrainian people have risen against us out of sheer war weariness. There is only one response to such treachery. The wider stakes are clear: With the elimination of any Ukrainian forces significant enough to pose a threat, the rest of the country will fall under the Red Army's control shortly. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 64}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd12.xml", "RD Storming Dover '53", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. Over three years have passed since the Allies fled Europe from the city of Dunkirk, and now our carefully made plans are going into action. Your decorated forces have been specially chosen by comrade Stalin himself to land on the British mainland and secure the beaches at Dover. The wider stakes are clear: Do not disappoint us in your next battle Comrade General. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd13.xml", "RD The Sack Of London '54", "A city is not captured in a single blow; it is taken district by district under smoke and fire. The post-war settlement has collapsed into a new European conflict. This is the last battle, comrade General! The British capital of London lies before our glorious Red Army of workers and peasants. The wider stakes are clear: The Second Great War A summary of the conflict from 1946-1954 (The following excerpt has been taken from The Second Great War, a definitive summary of the conflict that engulfed the world from 1946-1954. The city rewards combined arms and patience; reckless attacks will leave your best formations buried in rubble.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["North Korea (1950-1953)"],
["ncampseo.xml", "Seoul", "A city is not captured in a single blow; it is taken district by district under smoke and fire. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. The Imperialist Japanese have been driven off our peninsula only to make room for capitalistic Americans - but only in the south. The people of North Korea have the full support from our comrades in the Soviet Union. The wider stakes are clear: Seoul is liberated, and the Southern army is in disarray and close to fading into chaos. A strong result opens the road to SUWON (30 June 1950). The city rewards combined arms and patience; reckless attacks will leave your best formations buried in rubble.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["ncamposa.xml", "Suwon", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. I see that you are eager to pursue the capitalist forces and destroy them, now we have the chance. They have concentrated just outside Seoul on the southern bank of the Han River and have blown the bridges. The wider stakes are clear: You are absolutely positive that your men have encountered American troops on the battlefield? A strong result opens the road to TAEJON (16 July 1950). Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [3, 9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamptae.xml", "Taejon", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. They have blockaded our ports and we have suffered the first bombardments from American aircraft. Reconnaissance has shown that the capitalists have deployed units in the direct line of your advance on Taejon, which might be of divisional strength. The wider stakes are clear: Sources say the American 24th Infantry Division has suffered significant losses and has retreated southeast to the Naktong River. A strong result opens the road to PUSAN PERIMETER 1 (5 August 1950). Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["ncamppu1.xml", "Pusan Perimeter 1", "Urban ground compresses the front and magnifies every mistake. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. The end of our campaign for liberation is in sight. We have driven away the capitalist forces of the South and United Nations down into a corner on our Korean peninsula. The wider stakes are clear: While we are struggling to get supplies and men to the frontlines you have pushed back the Southern army and inflicted heavy casualties on the Americans but we still find ourselves in a stalemate. A strong result opens the road to PUSAN PERIMETER 2 (30 August 1950). Secure the approaches, protect your supply route, and reduce the enemy's positions one district at a time.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamppu2.xml", "Pusan Perimeter 2", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. We have increased your People's Army's strength as best we could. Almost 100,000 eager troops are under your command. The wider stakes are clear: By 23 September the North Korean army, what was left of it, was in full retreat back towards North Korea by every possible route it could find. A strong result opens the road to WONSAN (10 October 1950). Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampwon.xml", "Wonsan", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. The enemy has crossed the border at the 38th Parallel and is now advancing into North Korea! While the fury of our people can be seen in every village, our People's Army is in bad shape after retreating for hundreds of miles. The wider stakes are clear: Get in this truck; it's me, Comrade General ! A strong result opens the road to CHONGJU (27 October 1950). Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampcho.xml", "Chongju", "The battle has reached the streets, where every bridge, station, and block can become a fortress. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. Now the people of China will support its Korean comrades in the struggle against capitalism. Our armies have been allowed to reorganize in Manchuria and for days the Chinese have massed forces just across the Yalu waiting for the right moment to launch a counteroffensive! The wider stakes are clear: You have stopped the capitalist advance short of the Yalu River. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward MAJON-NI (11 November 1950) or CHONGJU (27 October 1950). Secure the approaches, protect your supply route, and reduce the enemy's positions one district at a time.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [3, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamphon.xml", "Hongch'on", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. The combined might of the expeditionary Chinese Liberation Army and the rebuilt North Korean People's Army will destroy the imperialistic ambitions on the Korean peninsula! Unfortunately our advance is losing steam; even spirited citizens cannot endure this much longer! The wider stakes are clear: Oh yes, we have the capitalists reeling and a number of South Korean units have already shown signs of panic. A strong result opens the road to WONJU DEEP RAID (7 January 1951). Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampwdr.xml", "Wonju Deep Raid", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. Sorry for the interruption, Comrade General. We have reached the important communication center of Wonju. The wider stakes are clear: AFTERMATH The front stabilized at the end of January 1951 on a line 50 miles south of Seoul across the Korean peninsula. A strong result opens the road to HOENGSONG (11 February 1951). Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamphoe.xml", "Hoengsong", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. Since we are very vulnerable; we should avoid getting involved in their offensive and retreat some miles to a strong defensive position. This night, in cooperation with our Chinese Allies, we have resumed our offensive south. The wider stakes are clear: This UN counteroffensive in the central sector was continued in Operation Ripper which immediately followed with Operation Killer. A strong result opens the road to MUNSAN-NI (22 March 1951). Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampmun.xml", "Munsan-ni", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. You can see the advance that the imperialists have made. All has been quiet in the western sector and we have almost totally evacuated the region between the Imjin and Han Rivers. The wider stakes are clear: AFTERMATH Operation Courageous consisted of an advance from Seoul north and an airborne drop by the reinforced 187th Airborne RCT. A strong result opens the road to SPRING OFFENSIVE FIRST PHASE (22 April 1951). Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [19, 21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampspr.xml", "Spring Offensive First Phase", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. This is the moment we have been waiting for, Comrade General. The Chinese have prepared a huge force for an offensive aimed at destroying the capitalists! The wider stakes are clear: I am aftaid that you were not the only one, Comrade General. A strong result opens the road to SPRING OFFENSIVE SECOND PHASE (14 May 1951). Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [11, 16, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampsp2.xml", "Spring Offensive Second Phase", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. You must have heard it already at the Chinese headquarters Comrade General but let us go through the situation once more. The offensive directed at Seoul has been halted in favor of a new offensive in the central and eastern sectors where the terrain is more to our advantage. The wider stakes are clear: Then finally the truce talks that started in July 1951 culminated in a cease fire signed on 27 July 1953. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampgue.xml", "Majon-ni", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Korean War is shifting between rapid manoeuvre and brutal attrition. Since September we have left many troops behind during our retreat north. Partisan groups have been formed to harass enemy communications and other targets in its rear. The wider stakes are clear: Between 14 October and 1 November nearly 180,000 Chinese troops crossed the Chinese-Korean border and more were to follow. A strong result opens the road to HONGCH'ON (26 December 1950). Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Forward, Comrade! (1939-1945)"],
["forward0.xml", "Battle at the Chalchin Gol", "The line is bending, and this position has become the hinge of the entire front. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Your mission is to put the enemy over the river. Your troops: We have chosen some troops for you. The wider stakes are clear: After your superior win, Japan have sued for peace. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Suomussalmi. The objective is not merely to endure, but to hold enough strength for the counterstroke that follows.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [23]}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward1.xml", "Battle of Suomussalmi", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. You surely know, that we are at war with Finland at the moment. Your mission is to break through the finish lines at Suomussalmi. The wider stakes are clear: After your victory, it seems that the finish government has to accept a peace dictate. A strong result opens the road to Pocket of Minsk:. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward2.xml", "Pocket of Minsk", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. You surely know that the Germans have assaulted our country. You have the permission to evacuate the pocket in need. The wider stakes are clear: Well done, we hold Minsk long enough to take new positions. A strong result opens the road to Defense of Kishinev. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward3.xml", "Defense of Kishinev", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. The Germans and their allies, the Romanians, attacking Bessarabia. Stop the advance of the axis troops. The wider stakes are clear: Now we have enough time to prepare Kiew for the defense. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Odessa:. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward4.xml", "Battle of Odessa", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Army has launched its attack on Odessa in the last days. They succeeded in pushing our troops back. A strong result opens the road to Pocket of Kiev. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward5.xml", "Pocket of Kiew", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Your troops are threatened by encirclement. From the north the Panzergruppe 2 will show up every moment in the back of your positions and they will join with the advance guard of the 17. The wider stakes are clear: That was what we have expected from you. A strong result opens the road to Pocket of Brjansk. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward6.xml", "Pocket of Brjansk", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. It may be expected that they will turn northwards and try to encircle your troops. Try to evacuate your troops slowly but do not miss to defend Brjansk and your other targets. The wider stakes are clear: Unfortunally most of the Brjansk region was occupied by the Germans. A strong result opens the road to Tula Counterattack. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward7.xml", "Tula Counterattack", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Now it is time to take the initiative. Panzerarmee, which will attack every moment your lines south of Tula. The wider stakes are clear: You have won the battle, but the Germans are able to win the war. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward Closing the pocket or Destroying the Demyansk Pocket. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward8.xml", "Closing the pocket", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. After your success at Tula we could also break through the German lines north of Moscow. Your troops should now deploy northeast and southeast of the city and attacking the last German troops which hold the last position, in which German troops could escape. The wider stakes are clear: The German divisions in the pocket have surrendered after fighting a few days. A strong result opens the road to Destroying the Demyansk Pocket. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward9.xml", "Urban Warfare in Moskva", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. The Germans have advanced to the western periphery of Moscow. The wider stakes are clear: The German invaders were crushed by your troops. A strong result opens the road to Destroying the Demyansk Pocket. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation, and the outcome here will shape the tempo and resources available in the next operation.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward10.xml", "Demyansk Pocket", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Since our offensive in the winter we could encircle the X. Army Corps near of Demyansk. Now we know that the Kampfgruppe Seydlitz is on her way to save the troops in the pocket. The wider stakes are clear: Very good, the troops in the pocket was exterminated before the Kampfgruppe Seydlitz could save them. A strong result opens the road to Defense of Voronezh. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward11.xml", "Defense of Voronezh", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. After our successes in the winter the Germans seems to have their troops reinforced. Slow down the advance of the Germans, so we have enough time to prepare new positions. The wider stakes are clear: We had good chances to stop the Germans some miles before Woronesch but you have not used them. A strong result opens the road to Rzhew Meat Grinder. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward12.xml", "Rzhew Meat Grinder", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. We have decided to start a great attack on the salient with the target of destroying the defendsing German troops. Your troops should attack in the north at Rzhew, in the south at Sychewka and in the middle of the salient, break through the lines and destroy or capture the most forces. The wider stakes are clear: Very good, the Germans have suffered heavy losses. A strong result opens the road to Operation Uranus. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward13.xml", "Operation Uranus", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Your troops will attack from the south and the northwest the German and their allied troops. This troops will attack the Romanian front in the northeast and will support your attack against the Italian und Hungarian troops in the southeast. The wider stakes are clear: The axis in Stalingrad are now encircled and the Germans and their allied troops suffered heavy losses. A strong result opens the road to Battle at the Myschkowa. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 12, 13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward14.xml", "Battle at the Myschkowa", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. The fascists and their allied try to break up the pocket of Stalingrad. We could stop them at the Myschkowa. The wider stakes are clear: Now the distance between Stalingrad and the German front line is very high. A strong result opens the road to Blowed by backhand. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 12, 13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward15.xml", "Blowed by backhand", "Preserve the army today so that it can fight—and win—tomorrow. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Herr General, the victory is within one`s reach, or maybe not. The Germans have evacuated the area of Charkow and withdraw their troops. The wider stakes are clear: Fortunaly your troops could withstand the German pricer grip. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward Free Leningrad or Prokhorowka Tank Battle. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward16.xml", "Prokhorowka Tank Battle", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. The Germans are attacking our lines at Prokhorowka. Resist all Germans attacks and lead a conterattack against Belgorod. The wider stakes are clear: After your success our troops in the north of the Kursker salient could break to the German lines. A strong result opens the road to Free Leningrad. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward18.xml", "Free Leningrad", "Preserve the army today so that it can fight—and win—tomorrow. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. More then two years ago the Germans began with their blockade of Leningrad. The pitful population of the town had to feel the pinch of hunger. The wider stakes are clear: The Germans were driven back several hundereds miles. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Viipuri. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward19.xml", "Battle of Viipuri", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Due to the invasion of Western Allied troops in France the Germans have withdrawn many troops. Your next operation will be the attack in Karelia. The wider stakes are clear: I am gladly to tell you that Finland have sued for peace and now will support our troops. A strong result opens the road to Attack on Riga. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 38, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward20.xml", "Attack on Riga", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. After our success in Karelia we now want to free the Baltic states. Your tank army have the mission to attack the Germans in Riga and throw them out of the city. The wider stakes are clear: The Germans have withdrawn to Courland and are trapped there. A strong result opens the road to Courland Pocket. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward21.xml", "Courland Pocket", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. We have started several trials to elimenate the trapped Germans in Courland, but all attempts were not successful. Attack on the front between Liepaja and Saldus, break through the German lines and take Pavilosta. The wider stakes are clear: You we can free troops for the Battle of Berlin. A strong result opens the road to Manchurian Operation. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward22.xml", "Manchurian Operation", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Now we had to keep our promise and built a second front against Japan in Asia. Your troops should break through the lines of Japanese and Manchukuo troops in the east of the town and capture Changchun. The wider stakes are clear: After the Faschists your great attacks have left the Japanese out of the war, too. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward23.xml", "Smolensker Offensive", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. You will attack the German Heeresgruppe Mitte at Yelnya. The Germans are well prepared for our attack, but I am sure you will be able to break through their lines. The wider stakes are clear: We have gained a lot of territory and destroyed several German troops. A strong result opens the road to Operation Bagration. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward24.xml", "Operation Bagration", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Several armies will join the attack in Belorussia. Take the town and push forward to the west. The wider stakes are clear: We could not only free Belorussia, but push forward to the Vistula. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Silesia. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward25.xml", "Battle of Silesia", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Herr General, meanwhile our armies have arrived Poland. You should take Krakow, west of you which is hold by the 4th Tank Army. The wider stakes are clear: You defeated the Nazis before they can withdraw their troops. A strong result opens the road to Fortress Küstrin. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward26.xml", "Fortress Küstrin", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Take Küstrin, take positions along the river and build a bridgehead over the river at Küstrin. Enemy troops: Küstrin is hold by a garrison. The wider stakes are clear: Fortunately the German troops in the east are captured. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward Battle of Berlin or Breakthrough at Dessau. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward27.xml", "Battle of Berlin", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Your troops have taken positions along the Oder. In the north the 2nd Belorussian Front should take Schwedt and fight against the 4th Tank Army. The wider stakes are clear: Hitler is dead and the surrender of the Nazis is near. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward28.xml", "Breakthrough at Dessau", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. After some planning the general stuff has decided that we will attack the allied lines at Dessau. The allies have numerous troops at this front line, so, if we can break through their lines, the allies must withdraw their other troops. The wider stakes are clear: Your troops could break through the allied lines and they must retreat because of their losses. A strong result opens the road to Battle of East Friesland. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 7, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward29.xml", "Battle of East Friesland", "Several Allied formations are trapped in East Friesland and preparing to escape through Emden and Wilhelmshaven. Your tank army must reach both ports before evacuation ships arrive, while a smaller supporting force helps reduce the urban objectives. The defenders still possess dangerous armoured divisions, plentiful infantry, and air power; worse, you begin without a nearby airfield. Bring engineers capable of establishing aviation support, seal the coastal exits, and destroy the pocket before it can become the nucleus of a counterattack. Speed will decide whether this is an encirclement or merely an expensive pursuit.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 7, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward30.xml", "Battle at the Ruhr", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. The majority of the war production for the Western Allied comes from the Ruhr area. If we will be able to capture the Ruhr area it will be more difficult for the allied to get supplies. The wider stakes are clear: After your success we could capture whole Germany in a few months. A strong result opens the road to Battle in the Ardennes. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 7, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward31.xml", "Battle in the Ardennes", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. In what the Germans failed once we now want to success. In the Ardennes the allied have build the last defensive line. A strong result opens the road to Charge on Antwerpen. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation, and the outcome here will shape the tempo and resources available in the next operation.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward32.xml", "Charge on Antwerpen", "What looks like a local defensive battle may decide the fate of the wider campaign. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Your mission is to eliminate the last allied troops and occupy the harbor of Antwerpen to prevent further allied reinforcements. Your troops: The harbor of Antwerpen is secured by several ships. The wider stakes are clear: The whole German Reich is now under our control. The objective is not merely to endure, but to hold enough strength for the counterstroke that follows.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward33.xml", "Breakthrough at Dessau", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. After some planning the general stuff has decided that we will attack the allied lines at Dessau. The allies have numerous troops at this front line, so, if we can break through their lines, the allies must withdraw their other troops. The wider stakes are clear: Your troops could break through the allied lines and they must retreat because of their losses. A strong result opens the road to Battle of East Friesland. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [7]}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward34.xml", "Battle of East Friesland", "The campaign returns to East Friesland, where Allied remnants again crowd the ports of Emden and Wilhelmshaven under the protection of armour, infantry, and air power. This time the enemy understands the danger and is preparing a more disciplined evacuation. Drive rapidly to the coast, establish an airfield for your own aircraft, and prevent the trapped formations from slipping away by sea. The operation rewards a commander who can split the force without losing concentration: seize both harbours, close the pocket, and deny the Allies bases from which to reopen the German coast.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [7]}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward35.xml", "Battle at the Ruhr", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. The majority of the war production for the Western Allied comes from the Ruhr area. If we will be able to capture the Ruhr area it will be more difficult for the allied to get supplies. A strong result opens the road to Battle in the Ardennes. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [7]}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward36.xml", "Ardennenoffensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. In what the Germans failed once we now want to success. In the Ardennes the allied have build the last defensive line. A strong result opens the road to Charge on Antwerpen. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward37.xml", "Sturm auf Antwerpen", "There is nowhere left to yield: hold this ground and make the enemy pay for every hex. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Your mission is to eliminate the last allied troops and occupy the harbor of Antwerpen to prevent further allied reinforcements. Your troops: The harbor of Antwerpen is secured by several ships. Use terrain, entrenchment, and supporting fire to survive the first blow—then punish every exposed formation. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation, and the outcome here will shape the tempo and resources available in the next operation.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward38.xml", "Kuban-Bridgehead", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Since many months the Germans has the bridgehead at the black sea. We could push them back, but all tries to destroy the Germans and their allied failed. The wider stakes are clear: While your offensive we could push forward in the Ukraine. A strong result opens the road to Zhitomir Counterattack. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13, 37]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward39.xml", "Zhitomir Counterattack", "Enemy pressure is building faster than reinforcements can arrive. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. While we have refitted your troops the situation near Zhitomir have changed in a serious way. The Germans have started a counterattack with five tank divisions after we have recaptured Kiev. The wider stakes are clear: The German attack was choked off by your troops. A strong result opens the road to Brody Cauldron. Use terrain, entrenchment, and supporting fire to survive the first blow—then punish every exposed formation.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward40.xml", "Brody Cauldron", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. With your advance the encirclement of six German and Hungarian divisions is complete. We know that the Germans will try to break out of the pocket. The wider stakes are clear: The Axis have suffered heavy losses and your victory opened a way to Lwow. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Romania. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward41.xml", "Battle of Romania", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. After we made peace with Finland, we want to urge Romania out of the war, because with the loss of the Romanian oilfield the Germans will not be able to perform big resistance. You have to break through the Axis lines at Jassy. The wider stakes are clear: Soon the Germans will be as immobile as a 90 year old rollator-grandma. A strong result opens the road to Take Szekesfehervar!. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward42.xml", "Take Szekesferhervar!", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. While the Germans try to break through our lines at the Lake Balaton in the west, your mission is to break through the German and Hungarian line at Szekesfehervar. With the capture of the town the way to Vienna will be open. The wider stakes are clear: Moreover the germans had to stop their offensive at the Lake Balaton. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Prague. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic"],
["forward43.xml", "Battle of Prague", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Eastern Front is a war of survival and transformation. Berlin is captured by our troops. Now we want to destroy the remaining German armies in Czechia and in Slovakia and free Prague. The wider stakes are clear: You could break through the German lines and destroy the 8th Army. A strong result opens the road to Manchurian Operation. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 37]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [13, 20, 47]}], "eqp-atomic"],
["A Long Journey to Freedom (1848-1865)"],
["aljf_0.xml", "Prologue: Knechtschaft oder Revolution!", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. 20. 4. 1848, Prologue: Knechtschaft oder Revolution! (Slavery or Revolution!) places your command at Lieber Freund,. Lieber Freund, not much time to write, hastily a short note for you: I joined Friedrich Hecker who is negotiating at the moment with prussian general Friedrich von Gagen. Von Gagen wants unconditional surrender which we never will accept. The wider stakes are clear: Prologue: Knechtschaft oder Revolution! * BV ( Prologue: Slavery or Revolution! * BV ) we have to move fast, General ! Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 176}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_1.xml", "Der Heckerzug", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. 20. 4. 1848, Der Heckerzug (Hecker's Uprising) places your command at Lieber Freund,. ORDERS: Herr General, free all the Main Cities around the Neckar and take you radvance to the important City of Freiburg. Reinforces from every liberated City will join our Revolution Army and the german democratic Legion aproaching in the South. The wider stakes are clear: Der Heckerzug (Hecker's Uprising) * BV Well done, Herr General !...but the enemy is too strong, we have to retreat to Switzerland, waiting for a opportunity to continue the fight..... Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 176, "support": [175]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_2.xml", "The Palataine Uprising", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. 13. 6. 1849, The Palataine Uprising places your command at Lieber Freund,. Lieber Freund,...this is the opportunity, we have been waiting for: the Palatains continue the Fight for the Republic, and we have joined them. The Prussians have send some of their best troops, but in our hearts is still burning a hot flame of freedom.... The wider stakes are clear: The People of Baden and their whole army, except the High Command, has joined again our side! Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 157, "support": [176]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_3.xml", "The decisive Battle at Wagh\u00e4usel", "Enemy pressure is building faster than reinforcements can arrive. 21. 6. 1849, The decisive Battle at Waghäusel places your command at Lieber Freund,. Lieber Freund,...the superior prussian Army has pushed us back over the Rhine River, but the People in Baden, and their whole army have joined the Revolution again !...now, we are encircled by the enemy and we must fight for our lives and the Republic.... ORDERS: Herr General, many enemies in every direction..... The wider stakes are clear: The decisive Battle at Waghäusel * BV Lieber Freund, we've fought very brave, but the Prussians sent more and more troops against us... at last our front collapsed.... Use terrain, entrenchment, and supporting fire to survive the first blow—then punish every exposed formation.", [{"id": 1, "country": 157, "support": [175]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196, "support": [176]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_4.xml", "The St. Luis Arsenal", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. May, 10., 1861 The St. Luis Arsenal places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, since I have been here I spent many years as Teacher and Editor of a german Journal.... Me and my former Comrades have foundeed many gymnastics Clubs, Pubs, Factories... and Families... The wider stakes are clear: The moment we have broken the last resistance of rebels in Boonville our connection lines are secured THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES -----{end of secret telegraph depeche}----. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_5.xml", "The Boonville Races", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. June, 17., 1861 The Boonville Races places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, wir haben uns mit modernem material ausgerüstet, und ziehen laut befehl nach westen- wenn wir die rebellen aus boonville vertreiben sind unsere versorgungswege bis auf weiteres sicher.... ORDERS: General, we send you a ship to support your troops. hurry up ! we need boonville fast ! The wider stakes are clear: But now we have to advance to Missouri as fast as possible! Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_6.xml", "Flank them at Wilson's Creek", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. August, 10., 1861 Wilson's Creek places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, the northern border of Missouri should be safe.... but now we have to annihilate the last rebel units to secure our supplylines... General Sigel proposed to use one of our most successful strategies of the 48 revolution: General Lyon should occupy the enemy troops frontally and General Sigel and we will sneak into its back... The wider stakes are clear: Wilson's Creek * BV ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}----- THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON, Dear Sir, now you should advance to the interior of Missouri with caution. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_7.xml", "Battle of the Hemp Bales", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. September, 20., 1861 Battle of the Hemp Bales places your command at Lexington, Missouri. Lexington, Missouri Dear Friend, the Missouri State Guard is attacking us for 8 days now. We are loading our rifles and guns with red hot iron bullets but they soaked the hemp bales in missouri waters and our salvos won't light them up at all! The wider stakes are clear: Battle of the Hemp Bales * BV ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}----- THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON, Dear Sir, excellent ! Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_8.xml", "Spearhead at Pea Ridge", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. March, 3., 1862 Pea Ridge places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, our order is to secure Arkansas for the Union ! As we have won Missouri for us I think our meanwhile well established cavallery will free Arkansas quickly too... The wider stakes are clear: Another 300pp could be attained by capturing enemy blockade runners which will be put at your disposal too. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_9.xml", "Assault at Kernstown", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. March, 23., 1862 Kernstown places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, now the time has come to draw our attack into enemy country... I got command for our attack on Virginia...! The wider stakes are clear: Kernstown * BV ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}----- THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON, Dear Sir, we were able to secure this area.... but we have to retreat....General Lee is moving with a large army towards Washington.... Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_10.xml", "Retreat at Bull Run", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. August, 28., 1862 Retreat at Bull Run places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, General Lee fought his way trough all our armies and stands now close to Washington....but more bad news: the enemy uses our famous strategy and flanks us.... we must draw back to better positions.... An orderly retreat...: one of the most difficult manuveurs... The wider stakes are clear: 2nd Bull Run * BV ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}----- THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON, Dear Sir, great, we were able to stop General Lee's attack on Washington ! Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_11.xml", "Must hold Harper's Ferry", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The defeated revolutionaries of 1848 have carried their cause across the Atlantic. Dear Friend, we have been ordered to Harpers Ferry. A little town and important railroad crossing, were the Shenandoah and Potamac Rivers meet, surrounded by mountains... The wider stakes are clear: Harpers Ferry * BV ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}----- THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON, Dear Sir, very well done ! now we must try to move further into Virginia...! Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}, {"id": 2, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_12.xml", "Take Fredericksburg", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The defeated revolutionaries of 1848 have carried their cause across the Atlantic. The confederates had destroyed all bridges across Rappahannock River. We have been ordered to cross the river and attack the confederate positions on the heights west of Fredericksburg and the railway. The wider stakes are clear: THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES -----{end of secret telegraph depeche}----. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_13.xml", "Battle of Chancellorsville", "The line is bending, and this position has become the hinge of the entire front. The defeated revolutionaries of 1848 have carried their cause across the Atlantic. Dear Friend, we are sitting in the middle of nowhere, waiting for the enemy. They are somewhere in the woods. The wider stakes are clear: As special recognition the newly launched USS Moose is detached to your army corps...! Trade space only when necessary, preserve your reserves, and counterattack the moment the enemy's assault loses momentum.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_14.xml", "The Siege of Vicksburg", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. May, 19., 1863 Vicksburg places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, the president has attached the USS Moose to our army corps... So here I am again back to the Mississipi valley where everything started for me... The wider stakes are clear: We send your corps as reinforcement of our front. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_15.xml", "Gettysburg", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. July, 1., 1863 Gettysburg places your command at Dear Friend,. Our cavallery scouts have spotted a confederate reconnaissance unit near Gettysburg...expecting the mass of Lee's army to be close our troops errected provisional defense positions around Gettysburg in the last moment.. My army Corps originally was intended to support the South East but being near by chance we have to support our comrades in Gettysburg... The wider stakes are clear: Gettysburg * BV ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}----- THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON, Dear Sir, the United States congratulate you on this victory ! Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_16.xml", "Meeting at Bristoe Station", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. October, 14., 1863 Bristoe Station places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, I have only time for a short letter.... Now we are on our way to Manasas Junction and were marching all day long.... The wider stakes are clear: Bristoe Station * BV ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}----- THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON, Dear Sir, once again you have saved the Situaion and we are indebted to you... Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_17.xml", "Seamonsters at Charleston", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. February, 17., 1864 Charleston places your command at Dear Friend,. ORDERS: Charleston is a important confederate port and one of the largest cities in the CSA. Some of our troops have already taken position in the southern swamps. The wider stakes are clear: You have secured this part of the coast ! now we have planned your corps for reconniassance and sabotage missions in the enemy country.... Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_18.xml", "The Cadets in New Market", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. May, 5., 1864 New Market places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, Once again our old friend Franz Sigel has taken command in our corps.... we have not met for a long time and the first night we talked an drank beer together...it has really been a long journey from the battlefields at the Rhine river up to here into Shenandoah valley.... Our original orders were to defend our own railway connections and to destroy the enemy ones... The wider stakes are clear: THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES -----{end of secret telegraph depeche}----. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_19.xml", "Sigel's Last Command", "The enemy has filled the approaches with strongpoints, but the city beyond them is the campaign's prize. July, 4., 1864 Harper's Ferry places your command at Dear Friend,. When the confederate army under Jubel A. Early was approaching us, General Sigel gave orders to evacuate the city. We hear rumors that the High Command of the Army once again fell in disfavor with Sigel and that he will be replaced soon. The wider stakes are clear: THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES -----{end of secret telegraph depeche}----. Secure the approaches, protect your supply route, and reduce the enemy's positions one district at a time.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_20.xml", "Our Marines at Mobile Bay", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. August, 5., 1864 Mobile Bay places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, We spend weeks travelling down the Mississippi and once we arrived at New Orleans, we had to board ocean going transport ships. I was able to write and send this letter just before we left New Orleans for the Gulf of Mexico. The wider stakes are clear: Mobile Bay * BV ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}----- THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON, Dear Sir, the confederate fleet is nearly non existent any more... Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_21.xml", "The Siege of Petersburg", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. October, 25., 1864 Petersburg places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, our army corps has reached Petersburg...from here important roads and rails lead in all directions....but especially Petersburg controls the last working railway to Richmond... by now we only control the area east of Petersburg.... Trying to undermine the confederate fortifications south-east of Petersburg, sappers already created a huge crater in the rebel position. The wider stakes are clear: Some U.S.C.T and our Marine Corps will support you... Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_22.xml", "The U.S.C.T. attacks Fort Fisher", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. January, 13., 1865 Fort Fisher places your command at Dear Friend,. Some of my best units are formed from black men...Finally we conduct this war for them and for the freedom of all men... as we did in 1848.. ORDERS: General, we have to take these important navy bases under all circumstances... best land your troops on the peninsula north of Fort Fisher but keep some landing units for landing in th outmost west, after the sea has been cleared from enemies. The wider stakes are clear: Now move back your corps to Petersburg immediately and close the trap...!", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_23.xml", "Close the Trap", "A cavalry force wins not by battering the strongest point, but by appearing where the enemy thought no army could be. April, 1., 1865 Close the Trap (Ft. Stedman + Five Forks) places your command at ----{secret telegraph depeche to general}-----. Furthermore half of the liberated slaves from Fort Fisher wished to fight on with you: we have formed three regiments and have put them under your direct command.... If we close the siege and take Petersburg we have depraved General Lee from any action possibility. The wider stakes are clear: You and your corps get the honor to start our attack... Scout first, avoid prepared strongpoints, and use speed to seize crossings, junctions, and retreat routes.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_24.xml", "The Key to Richmond", "The railway is the front: whoever controls its stations controls movement, supply, and initiative. May, 9., 1865 The Key to Richmond places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, General Lee and President Davis flew to Richmond, capital of the CSA and their last stronghold. ORDERS: Sir, now that we took Petersburg, the confederates are retreating to Richmond, their last stronghold and capital of the Confederate States of America. The wider stakes are clear: THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES -----{end of secret telegraph depeche}----. Secure the junctions, protect the track, and use mobile firepower before the enemy can isolate your train or sever the line behind it.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_25.xml", "Final Assault at Richmond", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. June, 23., 1865 Final Assault at Richmond places your command at Dear Friend,. Dear Friend, it is now that we are in front of the lion's hole... the lion is hurted and has drawn back to the outmost corner of his cave... but he still is really dangerous..... may be even more dangerous then ever... before as he knows there is nothing to lose for him.... I do not know how this will end, but I feel this is the end of the war.. one way or the other..this is the final decision...", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["Hungarian Soviet Republic (1919)"],
["rhu190416.xml", "1919/04/16 Escaping from Zilah (Zalau)", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. Escaping from Zilah (Zalau) places your command at April 16, 1919. After our new, revolutionary government refused to retreat behind the new demarcation lines, the imperialist hyenas incited their capitalist lapdogs, the Romanian and the so called Czechoslovakian reactionists. They mobilized their armies and attacked our weak, inexperienced troops. A strong result opens the road to Breaking through Nyíregyháza. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190424.xml", "1919/04/24 Breaking through Nyíregyháza", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. Breaking through Nyíregyháza places your command at April 24, 1919. Our troops weren't able to stop the overwhelming Romanian attacks. We should retreat behind the Tisza River. A strong result opens the road to Szolnok: Securing The Bridgehead. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects. The Hungarian revolution is surrounded and running out of time, and the outcome here will shape the tempo and resources available in the next operation.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190501.xml", "1919/05/01 Szolnok: Securing The Bridgehead", "What looks like a local defensive battle may decide the fate of the wider campaign. Szolnok: Securing The Bridgehead places your command at May 1, 1919. The Romanians have reached the Tisza, and a smaller vanguard has crossed the river at Szolnok. The retreat must end here and now, if the main troops of the reactionists can cross the Tisza, our proletarian state will collapse. A strong result opens the road to Defending Salgótarján. Use terrain, entrenchment, and supporting fire to survive the first blow—then punish every exposed formation.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190509.xml", "1919/05/09 Defending Salgótarján", "There is nowhere left to yield: hold this ground and make the enemy pay for every hex. Defending Salgótarján places your command at May 9, 1919. While your troops defended Szolnok, the Czech henchmen of the capitalist warlords took Miskolc, the biggest industrial center in North-East Hungary. Now they are surrounding Salgótarján, the last city with steal factory and strong organized working class outside of Budapest. A strong result opens the road to Liberating Miskolc. Use terrain, entrenchment, and supporting fire to survive the first blow—then punish every exposed formation.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190523.xml", "1919/05/23 Liberating Miskolc", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Liberating Miskolc places your command at May 23, 1919. Tens of thousands proletars joined the Hungarian Red Army. These factory workers are eager to fight against the capitalist marauders and their mercenaries. A strong result opens the road to Liberating Kassa (Košice). Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190530.xml", "1919/05/30  Liberating Kassa (Koice)", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Liberating Kassa (Košice) places your command at May 30, 1919. Our offensive is going well, and our soldiers are eager to take a revenge for previous losses, another shiny victory would boost their morale. More importantly, there is a good opportunity to deliver a severe blow to the Czech marauders. A strong result opens the road to Bártfa (Bardejov): Reaching The Polish Border. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190609.xml", "1919/06/09 Bártfa (Bardejov): Reaching The Polish Border", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Bártfa (Bardejov): Reaching The Polish Border places your command at June 9, 1919. The Czech capitalists are in disarray, they didn't expect how strong the Red Army of workers and peasants could be when they get a proper training about the dialectical materialism. Now we have a unique chance to cut off the Czech defense lines and separate the Romanian and Czech invaders once and for all. A strong result opens the road to Defending Érsekújvár (Nové Zámky). Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190613.xml", "1919/06/13 Defending Érsekújvár (Nové Zámky)", "The line is bending, and this position has become the hinge of the entire front. Defending Érsekújvár (Nové Zámky) places your command at June 13, 1919. Ah, dear Comrade Commisar, have you got the dedicated copy of Lenin's The State and Revolution? Comrade Szamuely has just arrived from Moscow with the warmest greetings and this special present for you. A strong result opens the road to Szolnok-Mezöhegyes Offensive. Trade space only when necessary, preserve your reserves, and counterattack the moment the enemy's assault loses momentum.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190719.xml", "1919/07/19 Szolnok-Mezöhegyes Offensive", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. Szolnok-Mezöhegyes Offensive places your command at July 19, 1919. They promised the Romanian troops would withdraw behind the demarcation line declared on March 20 in exchange for our withdrawal from the Fölvidék (Upper Hungary). But the enemies of our communist revolution broke their words, and their Romanian mercenaries are still staying behind the Tisza. A strong result opens the road to Szolnok: The Collapse. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190724.xml", "1919/07/21 Szolnok: The Collapse", "The line is bending, and this position has become the hinge of the entire front. Szolnok: The Collapse places your command at July 24, 1919. Though we have managed to cross Tisza at three locations, and we have gained a large bridgehead east of Szolnok, our offensive has stalled. We suspects some of the former KuK officers in our rank have betrayed our Soviet Republic and delivered important intelligence to the imperialists. The wider stakes are clear: Unfortunately, the Romanians crossed the Tisza at Tokaj, the Revolutionary Governing Council has resigned, most leaders are fleeing to Vienna. The objective is not merely to endure, but to hold enough strength for the counterstroke that follows.", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["Bolshevik Cavalry (1918-1920)"],
["ccampore.xml", "Voronezh", "The steppe offers room for manoeuvre—and punishes every commander who hesitates. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. We have overthrown the Tsar but that has not stopped the capitalists, monarchists and other enemies of the people to unite, raise forces and march on our people's republic! Petrograd lies under attack and Siberia is under enemy control. The wider stakes are clear: The smell of capitalists fleeing from the people's army is in the air. A strong result opens the road to ROSTOV (6 January 1920). Your horses cannot replace armour in a frontal attack, but they can turn a retreat into annihilation.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampros.xml", "Rostov", "The steppe offers room for manoeuvre—and punishes every commander who hesitates. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. Your army has not been defeated and is close to dealing another crucial blow to the capitalist's cause in southern Russia! The capitalist armies are ever retreating further south. The wider stakes are clear: AFTERMATH: By the end of 1919 the White armies in Siberia, western Russia and the Ukraine had been contained and defeated by the victorious Red Army. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF VOLODARKA (29 May 1920). Ride around resistance, strike artillery and supply columns, and close the trap before the enemy understands the danger.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampvol.xml", "Battle of Volodarka", "A cavalry force wins not by battering the strongest point, but by appearing where the enemy thought no army could be. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. Finally all of your command has arrived at the new front in the west. The newly emerged Polish state has invaded our sacred territory both in the Belarus as here in the Ukraine. The wider stakes are clear: However the fighting with the Polish cavalry showed that the people's Cavalry Army is a superior army! A strong result opens the road to KIEV COUNTEROFFENSIVE (9 June 1920). Scout first, avoid prepared strongpoints, and use speed to seize crossings, junctions, and retreat routes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampkie.xml", "Kiev Counteroffensive", "Speed is your artillery: the enemy flank is open, but only for a few precious hours. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. A major offensive by our armies north and south of Kiev has pushed back the Polish bandits. Even blind people can see that Kiev is about to fall. The wider stakes are clear: The Ukrainian capital has been liberated! The people of the Ukraine are now free from the capitalists who have ruled them for the past few weeks. A strong result opens the road to DELAY AT ROVNO (1 July 1920). Ride around resistance, strike artillery and supply columns, and close the trap before the enemy understands the danger.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccamprov.xml", "Delay at Rovno", "Speed is your artillery: the enemy flank is open, but only for a few precious hours. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. Take anything from the country as you go. The people will help you and if they do not it is because they are still terrified of repressions by the capitalist pigs. The wider stakes are clear: Although you were held up near Rovno, the advance is still under way. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF BRODY (29 July 1920). Scout first, avoid prepared strongpoints, and use speed to seize crossings, junctions, and retreat routes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampbro.xml", "Battle of Brody", "The steppe offers room for manoeuvre—and punishes every commander who hesitates. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. The Revolution will soon liberate the rest of Europe and join with other communists all over the continent! But first we must concentrate on capturing Warsaw in the north and Lwow here in the south! The wider stakes are clear: The Poles conducted a flanking attack on Brody while our eyes were pointed only on getting to Lwow. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF ZADWORZE (17 August 1920). Ride around resistance, strike artillery and supply columns, and close the trap before the enemy understands the danger.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampzad.xml", "Battle of Zadworze", "The steppe offers room for manoeuvre—and punishes every commander who hesitates. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. Let me quote something for the French socialist newspaper L'Humanite from early August. Long live the Workmen's International! As you can see our struggle against the capitalists is not going unnoticed. The wider stakes are clear: It only shows the superiority of the people's army! A strong result opens the road to LWOW (20 August 1920). Ride around resistance, strike artillery and supply columns, and close the trap before the enemy understands the danger.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccamplwo.xml", "Lwow", "A cavalry force wins not by battering the strongest point, but by appearing where the enemy thought no army could be. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. Comrade there lays the old city of Lwow. It was the goal of the Tsar in 1914, Brusilov in 1916 and our goal in 1920. The wider stakes are clear: For three days blood was shed and both sides have suffered massive casualties. A strong result opens the road to BATTLE OF KOMAROW (29 August 1920). Your horses cannot replace armour in a frontal attack, but they can turn a retreat into annihilation.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampkom.xml", "Battle of Komarow", "The steppe offers room for manoeuvre—and punishes every commander who hesitates. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. A few days ago while you were busy trying to capture Lwow; the Polish imperialists started a counteroffensive pushing through the center of the line between Lwow and Warsaw. After their breakthrough they turned north and now the entire northern command is retreating in order not to be encircled! The wider stakes are clear: NOTEWORTHY: Because of the numbers of forces involved, the Battle of Komarow is considered the greatest cavalry battle of the 20th century. Your horses cannot replace armour in a frontal attack, but they can turn a retreat into annihilation.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampro2.xml", "Retreat from Rovno", "Preserve the army today so that it can fight—and win—tomorrow. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. Comrade have I ever told you why I joined the Bolshevik party? The Northern armies will have to retreat on their own to defensive positions while we prepare to strike again and then finally make the wishes of millions of proletarians come true! The wider stakes are clear: The capitalists in Warsaw realize that further struggles with the People's Republic will inevitably will lead their defeat! A strong result opens the road to KAKHOVKA (20 October 1920). Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr1.xml", "Kakhovka", "Speed is your artillery: the enemy flank is open, but only for a few precious hours. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. He stabbed the people's army in the back while we were occupied with the war against Poland. Now that those reactionaries have seen that the Revolution in Russia cannot be stopped, we can muster all resources to bring peace to Russia! The wider stakes are clear: Our people's armies are closing in on them. A strong result opens the road to PEREKOP (28 October 1920). Ride around resistance, strike artillery and supply columns, and close the trap before the enemy understands the danger.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr2.xml", "Perekop", "The steppe offers room for manoeuvre—and punishes every commander who hesitates. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. We have almost made it to the Perekop isthmus. If those Tsarists are willing to make a stand against the glorious people of Russia then they will do it there! The wider stakes are clear: Not only is Moscow happy with your results but also the glorious people's army. A strong result opens the road to SEVASTOPOL (11 November 1920). Ride around resistance, strike artillery and supply columns, and close the trap before the enemy understands the danger.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr3.xml", "Sevastopol", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. The First Cavalry Army is turning mobility into strategic shock. Their dream of a Russia full of slaves they can control is gone! There are clear signs that the capitalists from London will send the Royal Navy to Russia and attempt to evacuate Wrangel and his forces. The wider stakes are clear: Something that Wrangel wanted to take with him in his escape. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [151]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["The November Revolution (1918)"],
["n_kiel.xml", "1918 Kieler Matrosenaufstand", "The old order is cracking, but the streets will belong to whoever controls the arsenals, stations, and bridges. Germany's imperial order is collapsing from the naval bases inward. No one still wants war, but the government does not get it. It sends the German fleet into the final battle against the Royal Navy. The wider stakes are clear: Some 250 sailors met in the evening of 1 November in the Union House in Kiel and prevented the fleet from setting sail again. A strong result opens the road to 1918 Wilhelmshaven. Win the streets, keep the movement united, and ensure that the first victory becomes the beginning of power rather than the prelude to repression.", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_willhelmsh.xml", "1918 Willhelmshafen", "A protest becomes a revolution only when it can survive the first armed response. Germany's imperial order is collapsing from the naval bases inward. After Kiel, the naval base of Wilhelmshaven is now rebelling. Under the leadership of Bernhard Kuhnt, you are now the one representative for the Council of the 21, whom the revolution now badly needs Conquer the north, Aurich, Emden and especially the reservists garrison Oldenburg! The wider stakes are clear: In Wilhelmshaven-Rüstringen was founded on 6th November 1918, after a mass demonstration of over 20,000 naval and shipyard workers and other civilians a workers and Soldiers Council, with its executive organ, the so-called Council or the 21. Momentum is political as well as military: every captured district may bring new fighters, while every delay gives reaction time to organize.", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_frankfurt.xml", "1918 Der Aufstand erfasst Frankfurt am Main", "The government still has officers and guns; the movement has numbers, momentum, and almost no time. 1918 The revolt comes upon Frankfurt places your command at 7 November. The coastal towns are in our hands. Now freed Frankfurt on Main and conquer by this the city of Finance, or can Großherzog Ernst Ludwig of Hessen put down the rebellion? The wider stakes are clear: According to the Sailors' revolt in Kiel, the revolution spreads to Frankfurt There they formed Workers' and Soldiers' Councils and called for the abdication of Grand Duke Ernst Ludwig of Hesse. Seize the centres of communication, arm new supporters, and prevent isolated clashes from being crushed one by one.", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_berlin.xml", "1918 Ende der Monarchie", "History has accelerated. One seized station or one broken barricade may decide who rules tomorrow. Germany's imperial order is collapsing from the naval bases inward. When the Emperor heard of the revolts in Kiel, he orderd the 4th Jäger Regiment to Berlin. The insurgents have the working-class neighborhoods under control. The wider stakes are clear: He then fled to his Dutch exile where he signed the abdication on 28.11.1919. Seize the centres of communication, arm new supporters, and prevent isolated clashes from being crushed one by one.", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["The Defeat of Denikin (1918-1920)"],
["volarm_00.xml", "The Ice March", "What looks like a local defensive battle may decide the fate of the wider campaign. The Ice March places your command at Feb 23rd, 1918. Once I swore to defend the Tsar and my country. When we learnt that generals Alekseyev and Kornilov had gathered some men ready to fight the Bolsheviks, Anatoly and I were among the first members of the Volunteer Army. The wider stakes are clear: After weeks of fierce fighting and ruthless weather we've crossed the white hell and reached the Kuban, just to see that Ekaterinodar has also fallen into the hands of the Bolsheviks. Trade space only when necessary, preserve your reserves, and counterattack the moment the enemy's assault loses momentum.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_01.xml", "Tragedy at Ekaterinodar", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Tragedy at Ekaterinodar places your command at Apr 9th, 1918. However, Kornilov is determined to attack. The Bolsheviks are growing stronger every day and if we leave they'll eventually find us and crush us. The wider stakes are clear: And in the north, since the Don Cossacks have risen against the Reds and the German Army is getting close to Rostov, the power of the communists has been severely weakened. A strong result opens the road to Belaya Glina. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_02.xml", "Belaya Glina", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Belaya Glina places your command at June 28th, 1918. In the north the Communists are very busy dealing with the German menace and with the uprising of Krasnov's Don cossacks, so the Red Army of the Northern Caucasus is receiving very little support from their comrades. That has allowed us to retake the initiative. The wider stakes are clear: Although badly outnumbered, my troops have behaved at the battlefield much better than the Bolsheviks. A strong result opens the road to The liberation of Ekaterinodar. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_03.xml", "The liberation of Ekaterinodar", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The liberation of Ekaterinodar places your command at Aug 13th, 1918. My dearest Katya, After the murder of the Royal Family our determination to destroy the Bolshevik scum is stronger than ever. Now, in a matter of days, we'll liberate all this region. The wider stakes are clear: Ekaterinodar is ours at last, and our army is growing. A strong result opens the road to Novorossiysk. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_04.xml", "Novorossiysk", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Novorossiysk places your command at Aug 23rd, 1918. Novorossiysk is one of the most important ports in the Black Sea. If we take it, most of our supply problems will be solved. The wider stakes are clear: Most of the Taman Army Group has been destroyed or is trapped between the hills and the sea. A strong result opens the road to Stavropol. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_05.xml", "Stavropol", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Stavropol places your command at Nov 10th, 1918. However, the enemy's numerical superiority is so great that our encirclement has been merely theoretical. If the Soviet hordes actually behaved like a true army they could break our lines at any place and march wherever they pleased. The wider stakes are clear: Surely they'll merge with the 12th Army, that is currently dealing with a cossack rebellion against the Reds. A strong result opens the road to Grozny. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_06.xml", "Grozny", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. Grozny places your command at Feb 1st, 1919. There is no time to lose, because now that the Great War has finished and the Germans have retreated from Ukraine, the Red Army will be able to send reinforcements to the Donbass and Tsaritsyn. If we don't finish the Terek campaign soon we might find ourselves fighting in two fronts, something we can't afford. The wider stakes are clear: I wish there was a way to convince them to join our army, but I think it's unlikely to happen. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_07.xml", "Operation Manych", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Operation Manych places your command at May 1st, 1919. The attack of the 10th Army on the Manych was a very serious threat to us. When they took Torgovaya they could split our lines in two, and even Ekaterinodar was at risk. The wider stakes are clear: Our right flank is secured, and now we can finally help the Don cossacks at Tsaritsyn. A strong result opens the road to Tsaritsyn. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_08.xml", "Tsaritsyn", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Tsaritsyn places your command at Jun 14th, 1919. The cossacks tried to take it three times in the last months, and every time they had to retire with heavy losses. The Soviets have many of their best units in this town on the shores of the Volga, including infantry, trench defences, armoured trains, heavy artillery and even some war boats. The wider stakes are clear: We could defeat the Bolsheviks more easily, and even inflict them a definitive blow. A strong result opens the road to Oboyan. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_09.xml", "Oboyan", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Oboyan places your command at Aug 12th, 1919. At first I couldn't understand the reasons why Denikin sent me here, to the left flank of our battle front, in order to help May-Mayevsky, who had recently asked for reinforcements, because he knows that I dislike that man. Even worse, he's allowed his soldiers to behave almost as common criminals, bandits and looters, not very different from the Bolsheviks that are destroying Russia. The wider stakes are clear: Nestor Makhno and his army of anarchist peasants want to help the Reds now, and they have invaded Western Ukraine. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_10.xml", "Peregonovka", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Peregonovka places your command at Sep 26th, 1919. They may lack a formal military formation, but they've showed great initiative and knowledge of the terrain. They appear out of nowhere, wipe out some of our garrisons, destroy or steal our supplies, disappear on the plains, regroup and attack some days later in a completely different location. The wider stakes are clear: The Revolutionary Insurrectionary Army of Ukraine has ceased to exist, and only a few of their partisans have avoided death or capture.They'll never suppose a threat to our supply lines again. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 171}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_11.xml", "Orel: White avalanche", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Orel: White avalanche places your command at Oct 11th, 1919. Some of you were already under my command during the Ice March, when we earned the medals with the crown of thorns and saw Lavr Kornilov die before our eyes. There are those who, for a while, believed the Bolshevik lies and belonged to the barbaric Red Army, but were clever enough to change sides. The wider stakes are clear: The Soviet 13th Army has been virtually destroyed, Orel is in our hands and the road to Tula is open. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_12.xml", "Orel: Red storm", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Orel: Red storm places your command at Oct 16th, 1919. You could see with your own eyes how the survivors of their 13th Army ran for their lives when we took Orel. They know that their time is running out, but they also know that they won't find mercy in us. The wider stakes are clear: Our only problem right now is that we can't advance too fast, because our own lines would be overstretched. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward Tula or Kharkov. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_13.xml", "Tula", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Tula places your command at Nov 3rd, 1919. Somehow they have managed to build a defence line south of Tula, and they have sent six fresh divisions from the Voronezh and Tsaritsyn fronts. I'll need all my skill in order to defeat the Reds and continue my march on Moscow. The wider stakes are clear: In a few days the Armed Forces of Southern Russia will link with Kolchak. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward Moscow or Kharkov. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_14.xml", "Moscow", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Moscow places your command at Dec 12th, 1919. I know that it may sound strange coming from a member of the Military Directory that will govern Russia until the revolution is completeley defeated, but I simply can't get used to political affairs. In my opinion, those pointless discussions were mostly responsible for the fall of the Tsar and the coming of the Bolsheviks. The wider stakes are clear: Our army will march along the main streets of Moscow, that has finally awaken from this nightmare that has lasted two years. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_15.xml", "Petrograd", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. Petrograd places your command at Jan 26th, 1920. Lenin, Trotsky, Stalin and most of their leaders have hidden here, waiting for a general mutiny among our forces, something that will never take place, or for the arrival of any ship that evacuates them to any country willing to accept them. The British and the French are so tired of war that they could allow them to stay in their countries. The wider stakes are clear: I think that Grand Duke Cyril is the legitimate heir, but in the past he has behaved as a person unworthy of the title of Tsar. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [151]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_16.xml", "Kharkov", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. Kharkov places your command at Dec 4th, 1919. Due to my past defeat, in the following weeks Denikin only assigned secondary tasks to me. My failure has prevented us from taking Moscow and, possibly, has cost us the war. The wider stakes are clear: Our army will retreat, unmolested and with very few casualties, to safer positions. A strong result opens the road to Last days in Novorossiysk. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_17.xml", "Last days in Novorossiysk", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Last days in Novorossiysk places your command at Mar 12th, 1920. They've stopped their support to our cause and are preparing themselves to live in a world with communist governments. The Bolsheviks have taken advantage from all of this, and in these past months they've driven us out from most of Ukraine, the Don region, and the Kuban. The wider stakes are clear: We'll still retreat most of the civilians and some soldiers to Crimea, but we'll leave enough troops to defend the Taman and Novorossiysk. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["volarm_18.xml", "Perekop", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Perekop places your command at Nov 7th, 1920. The Bolsheviks and their anarchist henchmen are determined to throw us out of Crimea. It took them some months to find courage, but now it seems that the moment of truth has come. The wider stakes are clear: The loss of their Sixth Army has been too much for the Reds who, under British pressure, have offered us an armistice. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103, "support": [171]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["Sim Pobedishi! - The Red East (1918-1920)"],
["simpob_00.xml", "Until you find somebody: the Komuch offensive (I)", "The enemy's army is tied to the railway. Cut the line, and the front begins to collapse. Until you find somebody: the Komuch offensive (I) places your command at June 8th, 1918. Wishing to die, and being certain that my end was near, in the first weeks of 1918 I returned to my hometown near Samara, where at least I'd spend my last days with my parents and sisters. But it all changed when the Czech Legion, intending to leave Russia, revolted against the Bolsheviks, who had denied the Legion safe passage along the Trans-Siberian Railway towards Vladivostok.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [144, 189]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_01.xml", "Uncountable trophies: the Komuch offensive (II)", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Uncountable trophies: the Komuch offensive (II) places your command at August 4th, 1918. As soon as we took Simbirsk, Kappel started to plan an offensive to capture Kazan, against the orders of the Komuch, that still wanted an attack on Saratov. According to Kappel's plan, the People's Army and the Czechs would advance along both shores of the Volga and would attack the Bolsheviks from several directions, trapping them in the town or forcing them to flee. The wider stakes are clear: Just one month after we occupied Kazan, a massive Soviet counterattack forced us to retreat down the Volga, towards Samara, with our enemies on our heels.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [111, 144, 189]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_02.xml", "Harvest of sorrow: the end of the Komuch ", "Preserve the army today so that it can fight—and win—tomorrow. Harvest of sorrow: the end of the Komuch places your command at September 18th, 1918. Trotsky coordinated the Soviet counterattack so well that, even before our evacuation of Kazan was complete, the Bolsheviks had taken Simbirsk, and Syzran and Samara were already in danger. The Fifth Army, commanded by the Latvian Slavens, which had followed us from Kazan, was in the north, ready to cut the railroad at Melekess and encircle us. The wider stakes are clear: As 1918 ended, where would we find the strength, the volunteers, and the supplies to overcome the terrible Red Army? Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [144, 189]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_03.xml", "At the gates of Europe: Ufa", "The enemy's army is tied to the railway. Cut the line, and the front begins to collapse. At the gates of Europe: Ufa places your command at January 6th, 1919. Not surprisingly, they soon started to use the trains to secure their own evacuation, while our men in the front lacked proper equipment and reinforcements. And, on top of all, the Bolsheviks kept on attacking us, taking one village after another. The wider stakes are clear: Our troops in the south weren't so lucky, and before the end of January we lost the town of Orenburg. Control the stations, repair the line, and make the railway carry your offensive farther than marching columns could ever reach.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_04.xml", "Breakthrough: the Spring Offensive", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Breakthrough: the Spring Offensive places your command at March 1st, 1919. Our supply lines were still a mess, and many of our soldiers didn't have a decent training, but we couldn't wait any longer. In the north, our Siberian units would advance from Perm to Vyatka and Vologda, trying to connect with Yudenich and the British near Petrograd. The wider stakes are clear: However, in the south, the cossacks, outnumbered, without adequate equipment, and isolated from the rest of our army, hadn't been able to take Orenburg. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_05.xml", "Rush: the Spring Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Rush: the Spring Offensive places your command at March 14th, 1919. As soon as we cancelled our unfortunate winter operation against Ufa, Kolchak's staff started to plan our Spring Offensive. In the north, our Siberian units would advance from Perm to Vyatka and Vologda, trying to connect with Yudenich and the British near Petrograd. The wider stakes are clear: However, in the south, the cossacks, outnumbered, without adequate equipment, and isolated from the rest of our army, hadn't been able to take Orenburg. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_06.xml", "Song of the cossacks: Orenburg", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Song of the Cossacks: Orenburg places your command at April 17th, 1919. After recovering Sterlitamak, Meleuz and Belebei, Bugulma and Buguruslan were the next important towns that were taken on our way to the Volga. But our advance had some vulnerable points, and Orenburg, on our left flank, was the most critical one. The wider stakes are clear: Since we had already dealt with a similar situation in Orenburg, Kolchak sent us to liberate Chistopol. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward The tide turns: Chistopol or Clutching at straws: defense of Belebei. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_07.xml", "Clutching at straws: defense of Belebei", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Clutching at straws: defense of Belebei places your command at May 15th, 1919. I wish you never experience that ominous state of mind of perpetual sadness, when all your efforts seem pointless, and everything that you love and cherish seems about to die. That terrible disease of the soul during which even breathing causes an immense pain, until you end up envying the stray dogs on the streets, hungry and full of ticks, but free of worries. The wider stakes are clear: Because not only did we defeat the Bolsheviks. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_08.xml", "The tide turns: Chistopol", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The tide turns: Chistopol places your command at May 26th, 1919. The spring wasn't over yet, and it seemed that we were about to repel the last counterattacks made by the Bolsheviks. Victory was so close that I could almost grasp it. The wider stakes are clear: When we finally liberated Chistopol I felt a great relief. A strong result opens the road to We'll never leave again: Kazan. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_10.xml", "We'll never leave again: Kazan", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. We'll never leave again: Kazan places your command at June 10th, 1919. After taking Chistopol we spent a few days resting and resupplying, but we continued our offensive as soon as we could. We were anxious to reach the shores of the Volga before the Red Army could recover. The wider stakes are clear: Denikin's forces had finally been able to advance into the lower Volga, and had taken Tsaritsyn. A strong result opens the road to Where it all began: Samara. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_11.xml", "Where it all began: Samara", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Where it all began: Samara places your command at July 14th, 1919. Unlike Kazan, their defenders had not built strong fortifications that could stop our assaults. We also knew that many Bolshevik regiments had fled to Saratov, and Kolchak had sent one cossack division to reinforce us. The wider stakes are clear: In the north, our Siberian Army had liberated Glazov, but it seemed unable to follow its advance and take Vyatka. A strong result opens the road to No mercy: Vyatka. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_12.xml", "No mercy: Vyatka", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. No mercy: Vyatka places your command at October 20th, 1919. By mid October all our supply lines were safe, from Vladivostok to the Volga, and we finally started to plan our new offensives. This time Kappel suggested to attack Saratov and join with Denikin once and for all. The wider stakes are clear: We left knowing that, without Vyatka, the Bolsheviks would not be able to defend Nizhni Novgorod and the roads that led to Arkhangelsk, which was occupied by our British allies. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_13.xml", "The Black Baron: Saratov", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Black Baron: Saratov places your command at November 13th, 1919. The Bolsheviks had fortified the city, knowing that its defences were all that stood between Denikin's Armed Forces of Southern Russia and us. However, they had been forced to retire many units from the Volga, in order to defend Moscow. The wider stakes are clear: Almost at the same time, the Siberian Army took Nizhni Novgorod and the AFSR defeated the Soviet Army in Tula. A strong result opens the road to Mousetrap: Ryazan. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [191]}, {"id": 2, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_14.xml", "Mousetrap: Ryazan", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Mousetrap: Ryazan places your command at December 12th, 1919. The Military Directory decided that Denikin's elite troops would lead the frontal attack against Moscow, while Wrangel and Diterikhs flanked them. Other units, including mine, would attack other points of the Bolshevik defensive perimeter, in order to weaken our enemies, prevent them from reinforcing the capital, and blocking as many Red escape routes as possible. The wider stakes are clear: The Directory ordered us to pursue them and destroy them before they could reach Petrograd. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_15.xml", "As though nothing could fall: Klin", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. As though nothing could fall: Klin places your command at December 30th, 1919. The Bolsheviks had decided to make a last stand near Moscow, hoping to delay our advance. That way, they would gain enough time to finish a strong defensive line in Petrograd. The wider stakes are clear: The Red Army was virtually destroyed after Klin. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_16.xml", "Peace through strength: Zhitomir", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Peace through strength: Zhitomir places your command at May 19th, 1920. During 1919 Poland was a formidable foe for the Red Army, that tried in vain to expand to the west only to be defeated by the brave Poles. However, the respect that we had for the Polish army, and the fact that the Bolsheviks were our common enemies for many months, couldn't hide the mutual enmity that existed between us. The wider stakes are clear: The Poles agreed to our conditions, and both sides signed a peace treaty in Minsk in June 1920. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_17.xml", "You've got to know when to walk away: farewell to Ufa", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. You've got to know when to walk away: farewell to Ufa places your command at May 29th, 1919. Rumours indicated that part of the Turkestan Army had crossed the river Belaya north of Ufa. If that was true, the Bolsheviks could cut our only retreat line in just a few days. The wider stakes are clear: Thousands of communist troops lost their lives at the shores of the Belaya, trying in vain to stop our evacuation. A strong result opens the road to Cry for the Romanovs: Ekaterinburg. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_18.xml", "Cry for the Romanovs: Ekaterinburg", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. Cry for the Romanovs: Ekaterinburg places your command at July 12th, 1919. Our defensive actions at Ufa could not stop the Red Army for a long time, and when they received fresh units from the west they resumed their counteroffensive. Their next objectives were Perm and Ekaterinburg, where they had murdered the Tzar and his family in 1918. The wider stakes are clear: Although, once again, our army was saved, the main result of the Bolshevik military operations against Ekaterinburg was the occupation of the main cities and factories of the Urals, the most important industrial region of Russia. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_19.xml", "The bear against the red wolves: Chelyabinsk", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The bear against the red wolves: Chelyabinsk places your command at July 25th, 1919. The Soviet 5th Army was attacking our Chebarkul-Irtyash line. Our High Command believed that our men couldn't resist for a long time there, so very soon the city of Chelyabinsk would be in danger, too. The wider stakes are clear: When August came the 5th Army was nearly destroyed, and only the skills of their leader Tukhachevsky prevented the Bolshevik divisions from a complete destruction. A strong result opens the road to Not dead yet: The Tobol offensive (I). Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_20.xml", "Not dead yet: The Tobol offensive (I)", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Not dead yet: The Tobol offensive (I) places your command at September 1st, 1919. All our efforts during the summer of 1919 had allowed us to retreat in order to the relative protection of the river Ishim. However, we knew that if we didn't launch a counteroffensive, the Red Army would destroy us completely before the next year. The wider stakes are clear: Our offensive ended on the right bank of the Tobol river, after having forced the Red Army to retreat more than 25 Russian miles. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}, {"id": 2, "country": 191}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_22.xml", "Better to burn out: The Tobol offensive (II)", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Better to burn out: The Tobol offensive (II) places your command at September 25th, 1919. The day that we were expecting finally arrived. We were told to follow our advance along the railroad, eliminating the Bolshevik resistance until we reached the river Tobol. The wider stakes are clear: And that was how the Red Army was crushed by Diterikhs and his Tobol offensive. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}, {"id": 2, "country": 191}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_23.xml", "Darkness falling: Novonikolayevsk\r\n", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Darkness falling: Novonikolayevsk places your command at December 7th, 1919. And then, on October 14th, they advanced again. The United Kingdom and all the other friendly countries were discreetly retiring their support, and were recommending us to accept our defeat and leave Russia forever. The wider stakes are clear: We managed to stop the Red Army at the Obi for five days. A strong result opens the road to Crying souls: The Ice March (I). Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103, "support": [189]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [20]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_24.xml", "Crying souls: The Ice March (I)\r\n", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Crying souls: The Ice March (I) places your command at January 4th, 1920. In front of us we had to deal with continuous mutinies, desertions and attacks from the partisans. Then he planned to go to the Baikal, hoping that we could continue our resistance there. The wider stakes are clear: At Krasnoyarsk we found some wagons and other vehicles that we used to advance faster without having to split our forces. A strong result opens the road to Once we were here: The Ice March (II). Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 0, "country": 189, "support": [103]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_25.xml", "Once we were here: The Ice March (II)", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Once we were here: The Ice March (II) places your command at January 27th, 1920. Although the Allied representatives in Siberia had told the Czechs to safely escort Kolchak to Vladivostok, when they ascertained that the Bolsheviks would oppose resistance, they quickly turned Kolchak over to the Political Centre. As for the Czech units that were roaming along the railroads, I wasn't sure if they'd be willing to attack us, but we didn't trust them. The wider stakes are clear: Kolchak and Kappel thought about continue the fighting in Trans- Baikal, but it was obvious that we didn't have an army anymore.", [{"id": 0, "country": 189, "support": [103, 144, 191]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["Czech Legion - Siberian Anabasis (1917-1920)"],
["acampzbo.xml", "Zborow", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. Now, during the World War, the time has come to liberate ourselves and rule our own country ourselves! The Habsburg K.u.K Army has suffered tremendous losses ever since 1914 and of the hundreds of thousands prisoners, a considerable number of Czech were part of that. The wider stakes are clear: In the battle of Zborow the Czech Legion captured 62 officers, 3150 soldiers, 15 canons and lots of machine guns. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 143}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144, "support": [153]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampkie.xml", "Kiev", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. The Bolshevik rule in Russia had resulted in a armistice with the Central Powers signed on 17 December 1917. To force the Bolsheviks to sign, the Central Powers have resumed their offensive actions and because of the complete dissarray of the Russian Army, they are pushing deep into the Ukraine. The wider stakes are clear: The Legion's 2nd Regiment took up positions at the bridges over the Dnjepr River at Kiev and held these for five days, until 3 March 1918, so that the bulk of the Czech Legion could retreat east.", [{"id": 1, "country": 117, "support": [64]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144, "support": [103]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampbac.xml", "Bachmatsj", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. On 3 March 1918 the Bolsheviks signed the peace treaty of Brest-Litovsk which made an end to official hostilities between Russia and the Central Powers. The Germans were close to reaching their new borders on the border of Russia and the Ukraine. The wider stakes are clear: OUTCOME At Bachmatsj the Czech Legion, in cooperation with Soviet Red Army units, stopped the advance of the German Army and could march its way east, out of the German occupied regions of Russia. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144, "support": [103]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acamptsj.xml", "Tsjeljabinsk", "Across this vast theatre, steel rails matter more than roads and armored trains matter more than fortresses. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. The Legion is allowed to get out of Russia using the Trans-Siberian railway. So the Legion was scattered over the railway between Penza and the Urals in May 1918. The wider stakes are clear: Still the Legion was scattered from Penza, west of the Volga River, to Tsjeljabinsk, east of the Urals... Control the stations, repair the line, and make the railway carry your offensive farther than marching columns could ever reach.", [{"id": 1, "country": 103, "support": [187]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampsam.xml", "Samara", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. After breaking with the Soviet authorities, the Czech Legion started to take over city after city along the railroads towards Wladiwostok. As it was still dispersed from east of the Urals in the east to almost the Volga River in the west. The wider stakes are clear: OUTCOME The Legion successfuly occupied Samara and was threatening more Russian cities along the Volga. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 103}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144, "support": [100]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampkaz.xml", "Kazan", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. In the process of securing its own fate, the Czech Legion was capturing various cities. Within weeks the Volga River was reached and the city of Samara was taken. The wider stakes are clear: Furthermore, the loss of Kazan shocked Soviet authorities in Moscow and the Czech Legion was seen as one of the many enemies of the Communist rule in Russia. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 103}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["acampoms.xml", "Omsk", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. The autumn of 1918 brought good news to the Czech Legion. To reach its homeland, the Legion had still to cross Siberia, which was in control of White Russian power under Admiral Koltsjak. The wider stakes are clear: Some of the opponents eventually joined the Soviets. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 148}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144, "support": [100]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampsem.xml", "Semenov", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. Early 1920, the Legion was close to reaching Wladiwostok. At Irkutsk the Czech Legion traded the Imperial Gold Reserve and Koltsjak to the Soviets for a free passage further east. The wider stakes are clear: OUTCOME After several clashes with Ataman Semenov, Semenov left the Czechs for what they were and concentrated on the Soviet forces which were approaching. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 191}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["acampwla.xml", "Wladiwostok - The End", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. After two years of struggle getting through Russia, the Czech Legion had finally reached Wladiwostok and all what was left was waiting on ships to take them home, as initially there were not sufficient ships to take all back home at once. You have get to Wladiswostok by passing American and Japanese zones of occupation. The wider stakes are clear: OUTCOME After Wladiwostok was reached, it took months to get home. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 152, "support": [145]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampka2.xml", "Kazan - Red Offensive", "The line is bending, and this position has become the hinge of the entire front. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. The loss of Kazan had generated into enormous bolshevik activity to stop the Czech Legion from capturing more cities and advance across the Volga River towards Moscow. The Soviet assembled their Fifth Army under General Tukhachevsky, which later lead the invasion of Poland and become victim of Stalin's purges. The wider stakes are clear: OUTCOME The Soviets eventually captured Kazan and the Czech Legion would retreat. The objective is not merely to endure, but to hold enough strength for the counterstroke that follows.", [{"id": 1, "country": 103}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["acampufa.xml", "Ufa", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. The Legion's road home runs east across a continent in civil war. However, still elements of the Legion were scattered as far west as Ufa, near the Ural mountains, when the White Russian forces of Koltsjak were on the retreat under pressure of a huge Soviet offensive aimed at destroying the White Russians in Siberia. The White Russian Siberian Army has suffered defeat after defeat and is retreating towards to Ural mountains where it hopes to stop the Soviet advance. The wider stakes are clear: The White Russians lead defeat after defeat and near the end of 1919 the Red Army had captured Siberia all the way to Omsk.", [{"id": 1, "country": 103}], [{"id": 0, "country": 144, "support": [100]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["The Polish-Soviet War: The Red Advance (1919-1920)"],
["polsov_01.xml", "Approach to Wilno", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Approach to Wilno places your command at April 15th, 1919. But rebuilding of the state was halted by the Soviet attack last winter. Instead of the roads and towns that needed to be built, the army had to be sent in to stop the Bolsheviks. The wider stakes are clear: There are rumours that the Polish Army from France is on the way to Poland. A strong result opens the road to Assault on Wilno. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["polsov_02.xml", "Assault on Wilno ", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Assault on Wilno places your command at April 18th, 1919. We have just secured the position for the assault. Easter arrives soon so try to liberate the city before the coming holidays. The wider stakes are clear: Your next objective will be the city of Minsk. A strong result opens the road to Liberating Bialorus. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["polsov_03.xml", "Liberating Bialorus", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Liberating Bialorus places your command at August 4th, 1919. The next step is to liberate Bialorus and create there another independent state that would serve as an ally separating Poland from Russia. You will lead forces striking south and cutting off the Red Army units. The wider stakes are clear: With the Soviet Western Army in disarray, we'll advance further east to stronger positions. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Dyneburg. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [193]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_04.xml", "Battle of Dyneburg", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Battle of Dyneburg places your command at January 3rd, 1920. But General Denikin not only refused to recognize the Polish state, but he also asked France (former Russian ally and current Polish ally) to stop supporting the Poles as well! Because of this, Polish authorities decided not to support Denikin's forces and stopped all aggressive operations against the Red Army. The wider stakes are clear: It has been a difficult battle but in the end the Soviet army has been destroyed and we have forged an alliance with Latvia that will be very important in the future. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [59]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103, "support": [60]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_05.xml", "Operation Kijów", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Operation Kijów places your command at April 25th, 1920. Well, it's time to assault Kijów and hopefully inflict a decisive blow against the Red Russians. You must break the enemy line near Zytomierz and advance as fast as you can towards the east. The wider stakes are clear: Once again we have routed the Soviet Army and now the way to Kijów is clear! A strong result opens the road to Race to Kijów. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["polsov_06.xml", "Race to Kij\u00f3w", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Race to Kijów places your command at May 5th, 1920. It seems that they decided not to defend Kijów and instead retreated to the eastern bank of the Dniepr river. If we can occupy Kijów fast enough, we can prevent the Russians from stealing many Ukrainian goods, food and documents. The wider stakes are clear: Although Symon Petliura thought that there would be a Ukrainian patriotic uprising against the Russians, most of the population is indifferent at best. A strong result opens the road to Surviving the red tide. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [103]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_07.xml", "Surviving the red tide", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. Surviving the red tide places your command at June 4th, 1920. They are trying to surround and crush our 3rd Army and we won't be able to resist their pressure until reinforcements arrive. We'll have to evacuate Kijów but we need some time to organize our troops and retreat in an orderly fashion towards our rear defence lines. The wider stakes are clear: The battle was tough but your masterful defence strategy was successful. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Warszawa: Poland's last chance. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_08.xml", "Battle of Warszawa: Poland's last chance", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Battle of Warszawa: Poland's last chance places your command at August 13th, 1920. Again and again we have been forced to retreat and now the Russian Red Army is ready for its final assault on Warszawa. As the Russian troops cross the Wkra River and advance towards Modlin Fortress, our defeat seems inminent. The wider stakes are clear: It is most important to advance quickly to the east and recover our lost territories before the Russians have time to recover or the League of Nations forces us to sign an armistice... Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["polsov_09.xml", "Komarów, the last cavalry battle", "The enemy still has a line on the map; your task is to ride through it and strike the rear. Komarów, the last cavalry battle places your command at August 31st, 1920. Our pursuit of the retreating Bolshevik army has been quite successful so far. Now we have an opportunity to encircle and destroy the Russian's 1st cavalry Army, one of the best units in the Red Army. The wider stakes are clear: Although Budionny and part of his army were finally able to breakthrough our lines and retreat to the east, their losses were very high and I don't think they'll be a threat to us anymore. Scout first, avoid prepared strongpoints, and use speed to seize crossings, junctions, and retreat routes.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["polsov_10.xml", "Riding across the Niemen River", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. Riding across the Niemen River places your command at September 20th, 1920. After nearly a month of withdrawal, the Red Army is trying to build a solid defensive line by the river Niemen, near the town of Grodno. We must break that line quickly so that we can continue our offensive before the Russian defenses are completed. The wider stakes are clear: It has been a tremendous battle but finally the Soviets have been defeated and they have taken heavy losses. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103, "support": [60]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_11.xml", "Back to Minsk", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Back to Minsk places your command at October 9th, 1920. As a consequence of the peace talks that are taking place in Riga, it seems that a ceasefire is imminent. Continue your march to the east, towards the city of Minsk. The wider stakes are clear: I'll be glad to go with you to Wilno to offer our victory to Our Lady of Gate of Dawn. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["Ejercito Popular (1936-1939)"],
["gce1.xml", "Batalla por Madrid", "Madrid is the Republic’s political heart, and the Army of Africa has reached its outskirts after months of rebel advance. Militia columns, newly organised units of the Ejército Popular, and the first foreign volunteers must hold the capital street by street while the government struggles to create a real army from the chaos of July. The bridges, western approaches, and urban strongpoints cannot all be defended equally, so reserves must be committed with care. Stop the assault, preserve the capital, and prove that Franco’s drive can be broken before fascist victory begins to look inevitable.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [203, 205, 206, 210]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce2.xml", "Valle del Jarama", "The direct assault on Madrid has failed, so the rebel command now tries to encircle the capital from the south-east through the Jarama valley. If the crossings and high ground fall, the road linking Madrid with Valencia may be cut and the city slowly strangled. Republican formations and International Brigade battalions must absorb a powerful attack, counter local breakthroughs, and prevent the enemy from joining hands across the river. Hold the valley, protect the communications of the capital, and turn Jarama into proof that the People’s Army can survive a battle of attrition.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce3.xml", "Batalla de Guadalajara", "Italian troops of the Corpo Truppe Volontarie are massing along the Brihuega–Torija line, confident that motorised columns and air power will finish what the rebels failed to achieve at Madrid. Soviet advisers and Republican reconnaissance have identified the concentration, giving you a rare chance to meet the offensive before it gathers full momentum. Use the weather, terrain, armour, and mobile reserves to isolate the Italian spearheads and strike their exposed flanks. A decisive victory at Guadalajara can end the immediate threat to Madrid and transform a defensive war into the Republic’s first great triumph.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce4.xml", "Ofensiva de Brunete", "With Madrid secure and new Soviet equipment reaching the front, the Republic is ready to attempt its first major offensive. The plan at Brunete is ambitious: break through from the north and east, threaten the rebel forces west of Madrid, and force Franco to divert strength from the Northern Front. Success depends on speed before enemy air superiority and experienced reserves can stabilise the line. Punch through the initial positions, exploit with armour, and seize the key towns while your supply routes remain open. Even a costly advance may relieve pressure elsewhere—but only a clean breakthrough can change the strategic balance.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce5.xml", "Ofensiva de Aragon", "The fall of the Northern Front draws closer, and the Republic must force the enemy to look away from Asturias and Cantabria. A new offensive in Aragón aims toward Zaragoza, but the open ground, dispersed Republican formations, and rapid rebel counterattacks make the operation dangerously fragile. Advance through weak sectors, secure Belchite and the surrounding communications, and prevent local successes from being isolated. The campaign will reward commanders who keep their forces concentrated and recognise when the main objective is slipping away. A secondary victory may still buy time, morale, and political value for the Republic.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce6.xml", "Batalla de Teruel", "The Northern Front has collapsed and the rebel armies are preparing to drive toward the Mediterranean, threatening Valencia and the territory that still links the Republic together. To seize the initiative in winter, the People’s Army will attack the exposed city of Teruel before the enemy can complete its plans. The battle will be fought through freezing weather, mountain roads, and fortified urban ground, followed inevitably by a powerful counterstroke. Capture the city, hold it against relief forces, and avoid exhausting your best formations before the enemy offensive has truly begun.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce7.xml", "Ofensiva del Ebro", "The rebels have reached the Mediterranean and split Republican territory in two. The Ebro offensive is the Republic’s boldest—and perhaps last—attempt to reverse the war. Under cover of darkness, the People’s Army must cross the river near Amposta and elsewhere, rupture a sector the enemy considers secure, and drive toward Gandesa before reserves and air power arrive. Engineers, bridges, artillery, and disciplined exploitation will decide whether the surprise crossing becomes a strategic breakthrough or a trapped bridgehead. Cross fast, widen the corridor, and force Franco to abandon the Levant.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce8.xml", "Contraofensiva del Ebro", "The advance beyond the Ebro has stalled before Gandesa, while German and Italian aircraft pound the bridgeheads and rebel reinforcements close from every direction. The great offensive has failed to achieve its strategic aim; the immediate task is now to save the army that carried it out. Conduct an organised withdrawal across the river, protect the remaining bridges, evacuate artillery and experienced units, and use rearguards to prevent pursuit from becoming a massacre. This is a battle of discipline under pressure: every formation brought back intact may be essential to the Republic’s final defence.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce9.xml", "Batalla del rio Segre", "After the disaster on the Ebro, Franco’s armies are pressing into Catalonia and the Republic’s position is collapsing. The command hopes to slow the offensive around Lérida by correcting the front and recovering two important power stations beyond the Segre. Your force must cross or fight along the river, seize the industrial objectives, and then survive the enemy’s inevitable response. The victory will not reverse the war, but it can buy time for civilians, units, and political cadres to escape the encirclement. Fight for every day the Republic still possesses.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce0.xml", "Batalla del rio Segre", "The war has taken an unexpected turn: Republican successes have destabilised the rebel rear, encouraged uprisings, and opened a new opportunity in Catalonia. South of Lérida, enemy forces are attempting to restore the front before the momentum becomes irreversible. Meet them at the Segre, defeat their counterattack, and turn a local operation into the collapse of the entire Catalan position. A clear victory will reopen the road into Aragón and place Zaragoza within reach. Maintain pressure, prevent the enemy from rebuilding, and make this river battle the bridge from survival to final offensive.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce1.xml", "Ataque a Zaragoza", "The successful counteroffensive has forced the rebels back from the Mediterranean, while the reopening of the French frontier allows long-awaited Soviet weapons to reach the Republic. Zaragoza now stands as the next great prize and the gateway toward Burgos. The city is protected by experienced troops, foreign support, and prepared approaches, but the strategic balance has shifted in your favour. Coordinate armour, infantry, artillery, and air support, isolate the garrison, and break the defensive ring without allowing the offensive to lose momentum. Take Zaragoza and carry the People’s Army into the enemy heartland.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce4.xml", "Ceuta", "The rebellion has collapsed across the Peninsula. Burgos has fallen, northern uprisings have shattered the enemy rear, and many rebel units have abandoned Franco’s cause. The surviving insurgent forces have withdrawn across the Strait to the Spanish protectorate in Morocco, where the war began. The final campaign leads to Ceuta: secure the coast, defeat the remaining formations, and prevent their escape or foreign reinforcement. This is the last operation of the civil war and the first test of the peace that follows. Finish the struggle, reunite Spain under the Republic, and close the road that carried the Army of Africa to the mainland.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["Zhukov: Red God of War (1939-1945)"],
["ga4_0.xml", "Khalkin Gol", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. STAVKA has decided it is time for you to break the stalemate at Khalkin Gol. The Japanese have been pouring reinforcements into the area, but, as you know, so have we, and we continue to do so. The wider stakes are clear: Most of the Japanese forces have been wiped out, the remainder being either caught behind our lines of advance or pushed back into Manchukuo. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [304]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_1.xml", "Chisinau", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. As you are now commander of the Kiev Special Military District, we have a special assignment for you to organize! As you know, the Romanians have consented to give us back the territory taken from us during the civil war, but, in disregard of the agreement, they are also attempting to take with them railroad rolling stock, factory equipment, and other supplies as they evacuate the area! The wider stakes are clear: Now the Romanians are protesting that we violated the agreement by using airborne troops and airborne tanks to disperse their army!", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_2.xml", "Yelnya", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. STAVKA applauds your decision in rejecting a defensive posture in favor of a more active stance. As a result, the German offensive has been brought to a halt here in the Yelnya sector. The wider stakes are clear: Your's and Rokossovsky's success at Yelnya has been the only bright spot against the German invasion of our country thus far. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_3.xml", "Istra", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. The lead German forces now stand less than 30 kilometers away from the Kremlin! Stalin has finally approved the counter offensive proposed by You and General Vasilevsky. The wider stakes are clear: Despite fierce resistance, the Germans have been driven away from Moscow, but the front lines are still relatively close, and more importantly, the Rzhev salient of Army Group Center remains intact. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_4.xml", "Rzhev", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. The desired effect of compelling the Germans to bring up four additional panzer divisions and one motorized division to deal with your attack, (thus effectively depriving their Stalingrad sector of the reinforcements they needed to deal with the Uranus operation), appears to have been accomplished. Therefore, Stalin has now authorized your order for the remnants of the 6th Tank Corps and three Cavalry divisions to break the encirclement... The wider stakes are clear: STAVKA has confirmed that the gains of Operation Uranus have now been consolidated, and there is no chance of a German counter-attack in the Stalingrad sector.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_5.xml", "Operation Iskra", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. I am sure that Stalin has already briefed you on the importance of this operation to our starving people trapped in Leningrad. They are depending for their lives on your leadership of the Leningrad and Volkov fronts! The wider stakes are clear: Once this second Road of Life is finished being constructed within the liberated corridor, Leningrad should be able to be supplied with all necessities until the Siege can be completely lifted. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_6.xml", "Operation Kutuzov", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. Your prediction made back in April has come to pass! The Germans have launched a massive attack towards Kursk. The wider stakes are clear: Despite fierce resistance, Your's and Rokossovsky's joint handling of the situation has sent the Germans reeling back under the weight of the Central front's advance, forcing the German command to acknowledge the failure of Operation Citadel. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_7.xml", "Kamenets-Podolsk", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. The joint attack by your 1st Ukrainian Front and Marshal Konev's 2nd Ukrainian Front has been approved by Stalin! The 2nd Ukrainian Front will move against Uman tommorrow, and then with any luck, we will end up encircling the 1st Panzer Armee in the Kamenets-Podolsk region... The wider stakes are clear: You have been re-assigned as STAVKA coordinator to both General Rokossovsky's 1st Belorussian Front, and General Zakharov's 2nd Belorussian Front... Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_8.xml", "Bagration (Choice)", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. Since you are now Stavka coordinator for both the 1st and 2nd Belorussian fronts, and we know how you like to be close to the front lines with your troops, Stalin has given you the option to decide at which front you would like to be... To choose the 2nd Belorussian path, go to Staging Area 2... The wider stakes are clear: Your order's for the 2nd Belorussian front will now be forwarded to General Zakharov. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_9.xml", "Bobruisk", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. Latest intelligence and recon reports show that the Germans have made extensive defensive preparations around Bobruisk, and have declared it a fortified area, nonetheless, we will proceed as planned. As you already know, the goal of this operation is twofold: breakthrough the defensive positions and take Bobruisk, and exploit any gaps that are opened, with the objective of forcing open a southern route towards Minsk... The wider stakes are clear: 5 divisions of 9th Armee's XXXV Korps have been trapped, along with elements of the XXXXI Panzer Korps that were not able to break out...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_10.xml", "Brest-Litovsk", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. Due to the staggering success of the Belorussian operations thus far, Stalin has decided to implement the plan for the expansion of the offensive to the Northern and Southern flanks. You will now suggest to Rokossovsky that he deploy the left wing of the 1st Belorussian front to the south of the Pripet Marshes. The wider stakes are clear: Stalin is also pleased that You and Rokossovsky were able to exploit the success, and as a result, continue the drive west towards the Vistula river... Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_11.xml", "Praga", "What looks like a local defensive battle may decide the fate of the wider campaign. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. Two bridgeheads over the Vistula have already been secured in preparation for the drive into Warsaw, and now that You and Rokossovsky are finished preparing, Stalin has given the go ahead for the last remaining key German bridgehead on the east bank to be taken, thus eliminating a dangerous bulge in the Vistula Front, which Stalin would like to have straightened out before starting any large scale operations.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_12.xml", "Mogilev", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. STAVKA agrees with you Comrade Marshal; the drive to capture Mogilev will be critical to the overall success of the Bagration operation. The German forces holding the Mogilev sector have a high proportion of very good units which cannot be allowed to reinforce either of the sectors to the north or south. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_13.xml", "Novogrudok", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. Now that the trapped German 4th Armee has, for the most part, been reduced in the pocket east of Minsk, STAVKA has issued new objectives for You and general Zakharov; secure the Novogrudok area, capture the key points of enemy resistance, especially Grodno and Volkovysk, and advance in the direction of Bialystok. The wider stakes are clear: Excellent work comrade Marshal!, You and Zakharov have acheived in 5 days what STAVKA had allotted 8-11 days to complete! Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_14.xml", "Osowiec", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. Now that you have successfully taken Grodno and Bialystok, STAVKA has issued new objectives for the 2nd Belorussian front; capture the fortress of Osowiec whilst securing the area and moving in the direction of Lomza, enlarging the bridgeheads in preparation for a further advance into East Prussia... The wider stakes are clear: Although the German defence line on the Narew River remains intact in the Lomza area, Stalin has noted the capture of the fortress of Osowiec and sends congratulations to the units and commanders involved! Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_15.xml", "Stargard", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. Seeing as the German counter attack has been blunted here in the Arnswalde sector with the result that the Germans are slowly falling back to their staging areas, Stalin suggests that you take the initiative and drive as far west as you can! This will assist Rossokovsky and the 2nd Belorussian front in clearing the enemy from all of Eastern Pomerania between Danzig and Stettin... The wider stakes are clear: Despite fierce resistance, you have managed to secure the Arsnwalde area and breakthrough past Stargard towards Altdamm and Stettin. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 303, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_16.xml", "Seelow Heights", "Urban ground compresses the front and magnifies every mistake. Zhukov's command career is becoming a sequence of increasingly vast operational battles. In view of the existing military and political situation, STAVKA has decided that the Berlin operation should be launched no later than April 16th, so here we are! Reviewing the plan once more: The main thrust toward Berlin and the capture of the city are entrusted to You and the 1st Belorussian front. The wider stakes are clear: On May 1st 1945 at 6:30pm, the final assault on the center of Berlin began. Secure the approaches, protect your supply route, and reduce the enemy's positions one district at a time.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["Spartacus: The Slave Revolt (73-71 BC)"],
["spa0.xml", "AC 073 - Escape from gladiator school", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. How long do you want to train great men, to slaughter each other in the arena? Arise - 200 gladiators are behind you ! The wider stakes are clear: Spartacus was born about 110 BC in the area around the middle course of the Strymon (modern-day Struma river, Bulgaria) 82 BC he was sold to Lentulus Batiatus, owner of a gladiatorial school (ludus) near Capua. A strong result opens the road to AC073 - Liberation of the surrounding area. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa1.xml", "AC 073 - Liberation of surrounding land", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Your escape from Capua was successful ! Now go get food and weapons from the transport and free the slaves of the surrounding area. The wider stakes are clear: So the Senate sent propraetor C. Claudius Glaber with only 3000 recruits. A strong result opens the road to AC 073 - Battle at Vesuvius (Schlacht am Vesus). Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa2.xml", "AC 073 - Battle at Vesuvius ", "Freedom lies beyond Roman roads, patrols, and legions determined to close every escape. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Spartacus - Months have passed and your followers entreched at Vesuvius. Gaius Claudius Glaber by now received the order to put down the rebellion. The wider stakes are clear: Propraetor C. Claudius Glaber drove with 3000 recruits Spartacus and his bunch before him, up to Mount Vesuvius, where he wanted to starve out the slaves. A strong result opens the road to Conquest of Nola (Die Eroberung von Nola). Gather weapons, free new followers, and defeat each Roman force before the Senate can concentrate its legions.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa3.xml", "AC 073 - Conquest of Nola", "Every captured weapon turns a slave into a soldier—and every victory brings thousands more to your banner. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Our army is growing, and the city of Nola lies ahead. The local slaves will help us in conquering by opening the doors at night. The wider stakes are clear: The army of Spartacus conquered the city of Nola, after slaves opened the town gates from the inside. Mobility and unity are your safeguards; division will let Rome destroy the revolt piece by piece.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa4.xml", "AC 073 - Battle of Acerrae", "Freedom lies beyond Roman roads, patrols, and legions determined to close every escape. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Nola you have left in chaos behind you, but your pursuers are already within reach. Furius, sergeant of praetor Publius Varinius, stands with 3,000 men at Acerrea. The wider stakes are clear: With 3,000 men, Furius saw towards an easy victory. A strong result opens the road to Battle near Salinae Heraclea. Gather weapons, free new followers, and defeat each Roman force before the Senate can concentrate its legions.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa5.xml", "AC 073 - Battle near Salinae Heraclae", "Rome expects another frightened band of fugitives. Give it an army instead. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Spartacus, now you have to prove yourself in the fight against Varius's legacy Cossinius. His troops have theur camp at Salinae Hercalea. The wider stakes are clear: After Spartacus had defeated Varinius lieutenant Furius, he encountered the troops of Varinius' legat Cossinius. A strong result opens the road to AC 073 - Escape from the camp of slaves. Mobility and unity are your safeguards; division will let Rome destroy the revolt piece by piece.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa6.xml", "AC 073 - Escape from the camp of slaves", "Preserve the army today so that it can fight—and win—tomorrow. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Spartacus, after defeating two of Varinius subordinate leaders, you are now almost surrounded by Varinius' main troops. It seems a pitched battle would take no good end. The wider stakes are clear: After the defeat of his lieutenants, Varinius was finally having a larger troop contingent to the site and surrounded the slave army at the camp of Heraclea. A strong result opens the road to AC073 - Conquest of Nuceria. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa7.xml", "AC 073 - Conquest of Nuceria", "Rome expects another frightened band of fugitives. Give it an army instead. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Now Nuceria lies ahead of you, but i don't think he will let you flee without further ado. So be on your guard ! The wider stakes are clear: On Spartacus way lay several cities, including Nuceria that he captured and reinforced his army with the freed slaves. A strong result opens the road to AC 073 - Destruction of Varinius at Picentia. Turn rough terrain and Roman overconfidence into weapons, and keep the road to freedom open.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa8.xml", "AC 073 - Destruction of Varinius at Picentia", "The Republic has underestimated you once; make that arrogance cost it an army. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Varinius is going to follow you to the back of the Moon. He stays together with his troops in Front of you at Picentia. The wider stakes are clear: Varinius was finally beaten by Spartacus and his Troops, his army was nearly exterminated. A strong result opens the road to AC 072 - Spartacus or Krixos. Mobility and unity are your safeguards; division will let Rome destroy the revolt piece by piece.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa9.xml", "Spartacus or Krixos", "Every captured weapon turns a slave into a soldier—and every victory brings thousands more to your banner. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. We are writing the Year 72 BC. The Celts are getting more and more aggressive and want to defeat Rome. The wider stakes are clear: As described, a Group of Celts under the command of Spartacus Friend and Subleader Krixos indeed separated to keep going to attack the Romans in their own Country. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward AC 072 - Battle of Mons Garganos or AC 072 - Battle against Lentullus. Gather weapons, free new followers, and defeat each Roman force before the Senate can concentrate its legions.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa10.xml", "AC 072 - Battle of Mons Garganos", "Every captured weapon turns a slave into a soldier—and every victory brings thousands more to your banner. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Crixus, prepare yourself for your first fight without Spartacus against the Romans. In front of you is the camp of Arrius. The wider stakes are clear: The Roman Senate dispatched a pair of consular legions under the command of Lucius Gellius Publicola and Gnaeus Cornelius Lentulus Clodianus. Gather weapons, free new followers, and defeat each Roman force before the Senate can concentrate its legions.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa11.xml", "AC 072 - Battle against L. Gellius Poplicola", "Rome expects another frightened band of fugitives. Give it an army instead. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. But his general Gellius' comes to avenge him. Can you put him to him to flight ? The wider stakes are clear: This is a fictional scenario, because Crixos never came to this. Turn rough terrain and Roman overconfidence into weapons, and keep the road to freedom open. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it, and the outcome here will shape the tempo and resources available in the next operation.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa12.xml", "AC 072 - Battle against Lentullus", "Rome expects another frightened band of fugitives. Give it an army instead. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. In front of you lies consul Cornelius Lentullus Clodianus with two legions. Behind you, Gellius and Arrius are moving up with two legions. The wider stakes are clear: The other two legions, running from the south up to Spartacus, were led by Consul L. Gellius Poplicola and his praetor Arrius, who had defeated Crixus. A strong result opens the road to AC072 - revenge for Krixos (Rache für Krixos). Turn rough terrain and Roman overconfidence into weapons, and keep the road to freedom open.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa13.xml", "AC 072 - revenge for Krixos", "Every captured weapon turns a slave into a soldier—and every victory brings thousands more to your banner. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. After you've beaten Lentullus, you hear of the defeat that Crixus had suffered against Gellius and Arrius. You couldn't put up with this accusation. The wider stakes are clear: Spartacus aligned obsequies for the fallen Crixus, where between 300 and 400 prisoned Romans had to fight against each other in a gladiatorial combat ATTENTION: NOT USE KRIXOS ! Gather weapons, free new followers, and defeat each Roman force before the Senate can concentrate its legions.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa14.xml", "AC 072 - Battle at Gallia Cisalpina", "Every captured weapon turns a slave into a soldier—and every victory brings thousands more to your banner. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. After you defeated Gellius and Arrius, the path to freedom over the Alps, where many of your followers have their home, lays clear. But is the way really free? The wider stakes are clear: Manlius made a stand against him Again the Thracian and his slave army won. Turn rough terrain and Roman overconfidence into weapons, and keep the road to freedom open.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa15.xml", "AC 072 - Battle at Firmum Picenum", "Rome expects another frightened band of fugitives. Give it an army instead. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Look at one: We know them yet! In front of us are the contracted troops of Lentulus, Gellius and Arrius, or what's left of it them. The wider stakes are clear: It took half a century that an enemy, the Visigoth Alaric, again stood an enemy army before Rome. A strong result opens the road to AC 071 - break the siege. Turn rough terrain and Roman overconfidence into weapons, and keep the road to freedom open.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa16.xml", "AC 071 - break the siege", "The Republic has underestimated you once; make that arrogance cost it an army. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. Spartacus, we`ve spend the Winter at the Söuth and consolidated. He has build up a mighty siege. The wider stakes are clear: At their first try about 12.000 Slaves died and it looked as if the fate of the Slave army was sealed. A strong result opens the road to AC071 Attack on the camp of the Celts. Gather weapons, free new followers, and defeat each Roman force before the Senate can concentrate its legions.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa17.xml", "AC 071 - Attack on the camp of the Celts", "Freedom lies beyond Roman roads, patrols, and legions determined to close every escape. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. The Celts that had separated from you need your help! Crassus redeployed his troops undetected to the close Camp and is attacking our Friends Gannius and Castus. The wider stakes are clear: But Spartacus was able to defeat the Quästor and fled to Lukania. A strong result opens the road to AC 071- Battle of Paestum. Gather weapons, free new followers, and defeat each Roman force before the Senate can concentrate its legions.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310, "support": [308]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag"],
["spa18.xml", "AC 071 - Battle of Paestum", "The Republic has underestimated you once; make that arrogance cost it an army. The slave revolt is growing faster than Rome can understand it. You march in the direction of Paestum. Certainly here are four Legions of Crassus - ready to fight. The wider stakes are clear: Crassus gave order to crucify 6.000 captured Slaves along the Via Appia towards Rome. Mobility and unity are your safeguards; division will let Rome destroy the revolt piece by piece.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["Viet Cong (1964-1975)"],
["nvc00.xml", "Raid at Binh Gia", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. Raid at Binh Gia places your command at December, 1964. Ah brave fighters of the Viet-Cong! Today will be our first action against our brothers, but do not see them as equals for they are traitors. The wider stakes are clear: Then we will decide on a course of action. A strong result opens the road to Escape from Vung Tau. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["nvc01.xml", "Escape from Vung Tau", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. Escape from Vung Tau places your command at December, 1964. Nevertheless, at the first light of day our agents in Saigon have reported that the puny so-called ARVN will sent a large number of troops to clear the Vung-Tau area of our men. The central office of the Viet-Cong thinks you must undertake an organized withdrawal to safer positions at the jungle. The wider stakes are clear: My orders are to tell you that Hanoi has decided that you and your command will be included into the North Vietnam Army. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc02.xml", "Attack on the Plei Me Camp", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. Attack on the Plei Me Camp places your command at October, 1965. As you know, in the central highlands near to the town of Pleiku, a couple of years ago the Americans constructed a so-called advanced combat base. Your task is to attack and take the camp. The wider stakes are clear: The government and the high command at Hanoi want to congratulate you on this great victory. A strong result opens the road to Ia Drang Valley. Avoid a fair fight, strike communications and isolated units, and withdraw before superior firepower can be brought to bear.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc03.xml", "Ia Drang", "A smaller force can still dictate the battle when it chooses where the battle begins. Ia Drang Valley places your command at November, 1965. Following your recent successes, Headquarters in Hanoi wants to continue the struggle. You will attack the advanced outposts of the Americans close to the limits of Cambodia. The wider stakes are clear: Although the enemy was better equiped, once again your skills were too much for them. A strong result opens the road to Military Region IV Crisis. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc04.xml", "Military Region IV Crisis", "Preserve the army today so that it can fight—and win—tomorrow. Military Region IV Crisis places your command at January, 1966. Our spies in Saigon have sent us information about an imminent enemy offensive of considerable size. Deploy your units quickly and take defensive positions to allow a retreat towards safer positions to the west in War Zone C. It won't be easy, since we need to save the local VC units. The wider stakes are clear: The enemy thinks he has occupied the so-called Iron Triangle, but many of our southern comrades are now hidden in this areas secret underground tunnels. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [0, 3]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc05.xml", "Asian Clash", "Strike hard, disappear quickly, and leave the occupier afraid of every path and village. Asian Clash places your command at July, 1967. As you know, commander, our positions near Tuy Hoa are right next to the South Korean troops who are supporting the western invaders. Some of our men, are shortage that exists an operation denominated by the Koreans like Hong Kil Dong, that consists of eliminating our defences in the zone. The wider stakes are clear: For now our supply routes through Laos and Cambodia are safe. A strong result opens the road to Strike on Kontum. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc05b.xml", "Strike on Kontum", "A smaller force can still dictate the battle when it chooses where the battle begins. Strike on Kontum places your command at November, 1967. As you know, our mid year operations in the province of Kontum have gone well, nevertheless there are still several enemy forward bases that we must destroy. Those bases are too close to our supply routes for Ho the Chi Minh trail and our area 609. The wider stakes are clear: For now our supply routes through Laos and Cambodia are safe. A strong result opens the road to Attack on Khe Sanh. Avoid a fair fight, strike communications and isolated units, and withdraw before superior firepower can be brought to bear.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc06.xml", "Attack on Khe Sanh", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. Attack on Khe Sanh places your command at January, 1968. As you know, our campaign of attacking enemy forward bases continues. Khe Sanh is the provincial capital and the key towards controlling our national Route 9. The wider stakes are clear: There is no time to rest since we must continue the offensive. A strong result opens the road to Tet Offensive - Hue and Da Nang. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc07.xml", "Tet Offensive", "Strike hard, disappear quickly, and leave the occupier afraid of every path and village. Tet Offensive - Hue and Da Nang places your command at February, 1968. Hanoi thinks we can take advantage of the two-day ceasefire announced for the Tet by striking now while the enemy is celebrating the holiday. One will take Hue, where the enemy 2nd ARVN Division's HQ and the MACV compound are located. The wider stakes are clear: It's time to get back to the jungle. A strong result opens the road to Laos Counteroffensive. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc08.xml", "Laos Counteroffensive", "The enemy owns the roads by day; your fighters must own the shadows around them. Laos Counteroffensive places your command at February, 1971. Once again we need you to re-start the offensive against the enemy. They are trying to cut our supply lines in that country's jungle. The wider stakes are clear: The ARVN has been kicked out of Laos. A strong result opens the road to Battle of Kontum. Your victory will be measured in disrupted movement, captured supplies, and fighters who live to strike again.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc09.xml", "Battle of Kontum", "A smaller force can still dictate the battle when it chooses where the battle begins. Battle of Kontum places your command at May, 1972. Continuing with our campaign of harassment on our southern capitalist enemies, the next step now is to strike the South Vietnam on their home soil! This operation is to attack and capture the provincial capital city of Kontum. The wider stakes are clear: Once again you have cleared our enemies from Kontum. A strong result opens the road to Liberation of Saigon. Use concealment, local mobility, and carefully chosen objectives to turn a raid into a strategic embarrassment.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc10.xml", "Liberation of Saigon", "A smaller force can still dictate the battle when it chooses where the battle begins. Liberation of Saigon places your command at April, 1975. The northern part of South Vietnam has been cleared of enemies by the People's Army of Vietnam. Hue and Da Nang along other key cities have been also liberated and now it's time for the heart of South Vietnam: Saigon! The wider stakes are clear: The Viet Cong flag has been raised over Independence Palace. Avoid a fair fight, strike communications and isolated units, and withdraw before superior firepower can be brought to bear.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["Soviet Black Sea Fleet (1941-1944)"],
["rcampfa1.xml", "Falciu 1", "The coast has become a battlefield, and every harbor, convoy, and battery now matters. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. Today fascist forces from Germany have attacked our borders, from the Baltic to the Ukraine. Our Red Army is the biggest army in the world and we have more tanks and aircraft than any other country. The wider stakes are clear: You have shown that it is a mistake to think the Red Army is an easy prey! Coordinate ships, aircraft, coastal guns, and landing forces carefully; one exposed transport can undo the entire plan.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampfa2.xml", "Falciu 2", "Control of the water will decide whether the army ashore is supplied, reinforced, or abandoned. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. North of the Pripjat Marshes the front has collapsed. However south of it, we have our front intact but are slowly being pushed back. The wider stakes are clear: Furious fights have shown the tenacity of the Red Army in war! Coordinate ships, aircraft, coastal guns, and landing forces carefully; one exposed transport can undo the entire plan.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampki1.xml", "Kishenev", "The coast has become a battlefield, and every harbor, convoy, and battery now matters. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. The Germans have broken through our lines and are advancing with high speed. However, to their south, the Romanians have still not managed a breakthrough thanks to your men. Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds, and the outcome here will shape the tempo and resources available in the next operation.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampode.xml", "Odessa 1941", "At sea there are no safe flanks—only range, weather, and the next enemy aircraft overhead. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. The Fascists are near Leningrad and Smolensk in the north and Kiev in the south. Here, near the Black Sea coast, the Romanian fascists with help of their German allies have advanced to the port of Odessa which is an important base for our Black Sea Fleet. Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampper.xml", "Perekop", "Control of the water will decide whether the army ashore is supplied, reinforced, or abandoned. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. Although Odessa is still in our hands, the enemy rushes further east. At Kiev we have suffered enormous defeats with the losses of hundreds of thousands of soldiers. The wider stakes are clear: We have most of the Perekop peninsula back under control. Weather and range are as dangerous as the enemy—commit your vessels with precision, not bravado.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampro1.xml", "Rostov 1941", "The coast has become a battlefield, and every harbor, convoy, and battery now matters. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. In the south the fascists have captured Odessa, broken through into the Crimea, and days ago Rostov. We cannot allow the enemy to hold this position. The wider stakes are clear: However many of the almost entrapped Germans managed to retreat and built up a defensive winter line at the Mius River, still tens of kilometers west of Rostov! Weather and range are as dangerous as the enemy—commit your vessels with precision, not bravado.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [37]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampker.xml", "Kerch", "Sevastopol remains under siege, and the Axis occupation of Crimea threatens to isolate the fortress completely. A double amphibious operation at Kerch and Feodosiya will force the enemy to divert troops from the western peninsula. Your force lands around Kerch from the Taman coast, where scattered German defenders will attempt to contain the beaches until reserves arrive. Put troops ashore quickly, secure the port and road network, and defeat the counterattack before the landing becomes a trapped bridgehead. Success will open the Kerch Peninsula and relieve pressure on Sevastopol.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampfeo.xml", "Feodosiya", "The second half of the Crimean landing strikes at Feodosiya, the key junction between the Kerch Peninsula and the wider Crimea. From the Taman coast, naval transports must deliver infantry and support weapons onto beaches that are thinly defended but certain to attract a rapid German response. Seize the town, port, and inland routes before the enemy can build a blocking line across the peninsula. A fast advance will link the Feodosiya and Kerch lodgements, threaten Axis communications, and draw forces away from besieged Sevastopol. Delay will leave both landings isolated.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampcho.xml", "Crimea Choice", "The operation depends on ships, shore guns, and troops fighting as one force. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. This is not a regular scenario but a so called 'player choice scenario'. You can choose which one it will be: Kerch of Feodosiya. The wider stakes are clear: TACTICAL VICTORY You have chosen to play Feodosiya. Coordinate ships, aircraft, coastal guns, and landing forces carefully; one exposed transport can undo the entire plan.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampsev.xml", "Sevastopol 1942", "The operation depends on ships, shore guns, and troops fighting as one force. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. Despite our initial successes in our Winter offensive, it has failed to defeat the fascist invaders. With the start of spring they have regained their initiative and at the moment are preparing a final assault on the fortress city of Sevastopol which is being cut off from our lines since last year. Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampno1.xml", "Novorossiysk 1", "The operation depends on ships, shore guns, and troops fighting as one force. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. We expected the fascists to strike against Moskva, our capital, but they have attacked in the south. Within weeks they had reached the Don River and Stalingrad on the Volga River. The wider stakes are clear: You have stopped the fascist advance on the coastal road. Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13, 61]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampsuc.xml", "Suchumi", "The operation depends on ships, shore guns, and troops fighting as one force. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. THe enemy's advance on the coastal road has been halted and that saves many Black Sea ports still in our hands free from an attack on one side. However the German advance has penetrated deep into the southern steppes and has reached the foot of the Caucasus mountain range. The wider stakes are clear: The fascist advance on Suchumi has been stopped. Weather and range are as dangerous as the enemy—commit your vessels with precision, not bravado.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampor1.xml", "Ordzhonikidze 1", "Control of the water will decide whether the army ashore is supplied, reinforced, or abandoned. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. The situation at the fronts is critical. And in the Caucasus Army the German First Panzer Army has refueled its offensive over the Terek River towards Grozny, and Baku where the oilfields are. The wider stakes are clear: You have effectively halted the fascist advance on Ordzhonikidze by not only stopping them in the city suburbs but even more by encircling them from behind! Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampor2.xml", "Ordzhonikidze 2", "At sea there are no safe flanks—only range, weather, and the next enemy aircraft overhead. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. Of all sectors of the front, from Leningrad to Moscow and to Stalingrad, just here at Ordzhonikidze, we have the initiative, comrade. You have saved Ordzhonikidze from an immediately enemy invasion and cut off the supply lines for the fascist forces at Ordzhonikidze. The wider stakes are clear: Although a considerable number of Germans managed to get to their own lines, we are preparing to liberate the region in our upcoming winter offensive! Coordinate ships, aircraft, coastal guns, and landing forces carefully; one exposed transport can undo the entire plan.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampmai.xml", "Maikop", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. And in the Caucasus the Germans are slowly retreating. We started our winter offensive to liberate the Caucasus region all the way up to Novorossiysk and Rostov, some weeks ago. The wider stakes are clear: We have destroyed many Romanian, Hungarian and Italian units in battles near the Don River. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampro2.xml", "Rostov 1943", "The operation depends on ships, shore guns, and troops fighting as one force. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. We have advanced hundreds of kilometers and we once again stand at the gates of Rostov. It is vital that we capture this gate to the Caucasus as soon as possible, because still not all German units have retreated over the Don, back into the Ukraine. The wider stakes are clear: We have liberated Rostov again and the Caucasus has been liberated entirely but for the Kuban region. Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampno2.xml", "Novorossiysk 2", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. We are happy to hold down the Germans. More south, the enemy is still holding the Kuban region, of which the Taman peninsula is only a few miles away from the Kerch peninsula of the Crimea. The wider stakes are clear: Attacks on all of the fascist Kuban positions are continuing as we speak! Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampkry.xml", "Krymskaya", "The coast has become a battlefield, and every harbor, convoy, and battery now matters. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. After a month of ferious attacks we have not breached the fascist front. We have only advanced several miles, and the cities of Novorossiysk and Krasnodar are still in enemy hands. The wider stakes are clear: On the other hand, the enemy was not able to destroy the Novorossiysk bridgehead either. Coordinate ships, aircraft, coastal guns, and landing forces carefully; one exposed transport can undo the entire plan.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampno3.xml", "Novocross", "The operation depends on ships, shore guns, and troops fighting as one force. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. And finally, after months of preparations, we are in position for a full-scale attack on the fascist perimeter. We must follow and make the enemy see that the Red Army has arisen from its ashes! The wider stakes are clear: Finally we have broken through and have liberated Novorossiysk! Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13, 61]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcamptam.xml", "Taman", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. Those were quite some days, comrade. Krasnodar and Novorossiysk have been liberated and the fascists cowards are fleeing towards the Taman peninsula where they should be evacuated to the Crimea. The wider stakes are clear: In the Ukraine our offensive is steaming towards the Dnjepr River. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampod2.xml", "Odessa 1944", "The operation depends on ships, shore guns, and troops fighting as one force. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. Our winter offensive has brought us on the other side of the Dnjepr River and Kiev has been liberated. We will attack near Perekop and force ourselves into the Crimea. The wider stakes are clear: After months of advancing, our troops in the Ukraine will stop large offensive actions as almost the entire Ukraine has been liberated now. Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampse2.xml", "Sevastopol 1944", "Control of the water will decide whether the army ashore is supplied, reinforced, or abandoned. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. A month ago we broke through fascist lines at the Perekop peninsula, the sole connection of the Crimean peninsula with the Ukrainian mainland. The enemy has retreated from all over the Crimea to Sevastopol which has been turned into a fortress once again. The wider stakes are clear: We do not even start counting the dead bodies in and around Sevastopol. Coordinate ships, aircraft, coastal guns, and landing forces carefully; one exposed transport can undo the entire plan.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampjas.xml", "Jassy", "Your force is exposed, the roads are closing, and every hour of delay narrows the route to safety. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. Since our spring offensives we have a bridgehead into Rumania over the Prut River, near Jassy. The fascists have taken blow after blow but somehow have regained their spirit. The wider stakes are clear: We still have our bridgehead over the Prut River near Jassy. Rear guards must buy time while the main body escapes; abandon cohesion and the campaign may end here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampfa3.xml", "Falciu 3", "Control of the water will decide whether the army ashore is supplied, reinforced, or abandoned. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. The biggest ally of the German cowards that invaded our country. Like our offensives in the Baltic and Byelorussia, we have made promising advances. The wider stakes are clear: The Red Army has encircled many fascist formations. Coordinate ships, aircraft, coastal guns, and landing forces carefully; one exposed transport can undo the entire plan.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampbuc.xml", "Bucharest", "The operation depends on ships, shore guns, and troops fighting as one force. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. Great news from some days ago: the Romanians have surrendered to the mighty Soviet Union and are now fighting against the Germans. However there are still Romanian fascists in the Romanian Army that refuse to surrender and remain loyal to their fascists leaders and the Germans. The wider stakes are clear: The fascists are almost as good as driven out of Rumania and now the Romanian Army is fighting alongside us against the Germans and Hungarians. Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [8, 13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61, "support": [13]}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcamprus.xml", "Ruse", "The coast has become a battlefield, and every harbor, convoy, and battery now matters. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. While the front against the fascists moves west, into Yugoslavia, Hungary, Czechoslovakia and Poland, your force will used in a special mission. Bulgaria and our Soviet Union have never been in war. The wider stakes are clear: However they are no match for our experienced veterans. Coordinate ships, aircraft, coastal guns, and landing forces carefully; one exposed transport can undo the entire plan.", [{"id": 1, "country": 8}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampsof.xml", "Sofia", "Control of the water will decide whether the army ashore is supplied, reinforced, or abandoned. The Black Sea war ties the front to ports, convoys, and coastal strongholds. The last days, we have not encountered heavy resistance. Most of the Bulgarian Army is deployed in occupied territories in Greece and Yugoslavia. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY Bulgaria has switched sides and the Bulgarian Army, as the Romanian Army, is fighting alongside us against the German fascists. Protect the sea lanes, suppress shore defences, and deliver troops where the enemy least expects them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 8}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61, "support": [8]}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["Red Star Over China (1927-1949)"],
["mao1.xml", "Nanchang Uprising", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. Today we will join the revolution against the ancient oppressors of the Chinese people and against the likes of Chiang-Kai-Shek. Some of our comrades in other army units will also join us in our glorious uprising against the enemies of the people. The wider stakes are clear: This has become the first major stronghold of Marxism in China. A strong result opens the road to Autumn Harvest Uprising. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao2.xml", "Autumn Harvest Uprising", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. The uprising at Guangzhou against the local warlords was successful and access by sea for Soviet aid was secured. Now, comrade Mao from Hunan is planning an assault on the city fortress of Changsha against the local warlords and KMT troops placed at that city. The wider stakes are clear: The uprising was very successfull here in Changsha... A strong result opens the road to KMT Annihilation Campaign. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao3.xml", "Jiangxi Soviet", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. It is well protected and hidden from our enemies by a heavy wilderness and bamboo trees. All the access points to our base are under continuous servalance and our Soviet GRU spies report that the Kuomingtan enemies and the Warlords are planning to eradicate us at once. The wider stakes are clear: Myself, together with Mao and our Komintern advisor Li-De (Otto Braun) are planning the evacuation of Jinggangshan. A strong result opens the road to Long March - Luding Bridge. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao4.xml", "Long March - Luding Bridge", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. We have escaped from Jingghanshan in our long march to the North. Today the Dadu River lies in front of us, and your task is to cross that river. The wider stakes are clear: We have crossed that damned bridge and many comrades have died, but their lives were not lost, they have contributed to the success of our retreat to save the Revolution. A strong result opens the road to Pingxingguan Pass. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao5.xml", "Pingxingguan Pass", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. 25-9-1937, Pingxingguan Pass, near Datong, Northern China. Now, the enemy is the foreign imperialist invader, it's time to forget our quarrel with the KMT for a while. The wider stakes are clear: The enemy division is completely scattered and our troops can continue to harass them. A strong result opens the road to 100 Regiments Offensive. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao5_2.xml", "100 Regiments Offensive", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. 100 Regiments Offensive places your command at 1-11-1940, Shanzi, North-Central China. Again, the central committee of the ChCP has agreed to launch another guerrilla assault on the Japanese rearguard in co-operation with our Kuomingtan allies. But China is calling for Chinese action against the invaders, and that's what we are going to carry out. The wider stakes are clear: All the mission objectives were achieved before the Japanese could send reinforcements to this area. A strong result opens the road to Central Plains Breakout. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao6.xml", "Central Plains Breakout", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. I hope the lessons you have reciently taken in the USSR about the modern warfare will be useful for us now. As you know, the Soviet victory agaisnt the Japanese in Manchuria the past year has opened the gate of the regular support of hardware and weapons to us. The wider stakes are clear: We must hope to counterstrike the dirty nationalists as soon as we receive some Soviet aid through Manchuria. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao7.xml", "Linjiang Campaign", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. Your actions were enough to support your upgrade decided in the ChCP council... Your first assignment as PLA's commander will be in the Jilin province, our base there is placed at Linjiang. The wider stakes are clear: In addition, we are now in a good position to attack Changchun, Jilin and Siping during the next summer offensive. A strong result opens the road to Summer Offensive 1947. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao8.xml", "Summer Offensive 1947", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. Orders from the central ChCP comitte: it's time to capture Changchun, Siping, and Jilin to complete the conquest of Manchuria. The success on this offensive is extremely important, because it would allow us to undertake further penetrations on to Beijing and Nanjing in the next months. The wider stakes are clear: This will be a big problem for the Nationalists, since their communications by train or by road from Manchuria to Beijing are now stopped. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao9.xml", "Winter Offensive 1947", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. Our victories at Changchun and Siping have decimated their men, commander, and you must put an end to the nationalist resistance in Manchuria. Your mission is to secure the communications between our base at Siping and our groups in the South, near to Shenyang. The wider stakes are clear: I'm sure we will be celebrating our victory over Chiang Kai Shek's troops during the coming year of 1948. A strong result opens the road to Pyongyang Liberation [Korean War]. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao11.xml", "Pyongyang Liberation [Korean War]", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. 25-11-1950 Chongchon River, near the Chinese border. Your next mission is highly secret and will take you to the Sino-Korean border. The wider stakes are clear: Pyongyang is again a communist stronghold, and we must continue to pursue and annihilate the UN forces. A strong result opens the road to Chosin Reservoir [Korean War]. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao12.xml", "Chosin Reservoir [Korean War]", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. 27-11-1950 Chosin Reservoir, N of North Korea. Your quick advance has created a salient in the enemy lines, like the one at the Chosin Reservoir. The wider stakes are clear: The North Americans have received a stinging lesson on the power of the People's War. A strong result opens the road to Hungnam Pocket [Korean War]. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao13.xml", "Hungnam Pocket [Korean War]", "This is not a rout unless you allow it to become one. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. Again, your smashing attack has left the enemy forces on the ground isolated. This is the situation at Hungnam. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY Some UN forces have escaped from Hungnam, but at least we can now continue with our advance towards Seoul. A strong result opens the road to Seoul: UN Counterattack. Every surviving veteran will matter in the battles ahead, so retreat with purpose and destroy what the enemy cannot be allowed to capture.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao13_2.xml", "UN Counterattack [Korean War]", "A city is not captured in a single blow; it is taken district by district under smoke and fire. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. 25-1-1951 The lightning advances of December and early January provide us with the opportunity to easily retake Seoul for the North Koreans. Our supply lines to China are long and are constantly being bombed and strafed by the UN air force. The wider stakes are clear: You have permission to retreat your armies behind the Han river to avoid future losses. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward Pusan Revisited or Spring Offensive [Korean War]. Secure the approaches, protect your supply route, and reduce the enemy's positions one district at a time.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao14.xml", "Spring Offensive [Korean War]", "Urban ground compresses the front and magnifies every mistake. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. It's time to go back to Seoul. We have deployed a large number of PLA and KPA units Northwards toward Seoul and with your armies nothing will stop us in our drive. The wider stakes are clear: The North Korean flag again flies over the city of Seoul. Your result determines whether the campaign continues toward Pusan Revisited or Taiwan Strait - Nuclear Crisis. Use artillery and infantry together, isolate strongpoints, and avoid wasting elite units in unsupported assaults.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22, 73]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao14_2.xml", "Pusan Revisited [Korean War]", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. Pusan Revisited places your command at 27-6-1951 Pusan, South Korea. Just like last year, the UN forces are again encircled on the Pusan Perimeter. Now, with the bulk of the North Korean forces are guarding the rear, we can assault the enemy positions without the fear of an assault on our back like last years landings at Inch'on. The wider stakes are clear: Korea is now entirely unified under the communist flag, and Kim-Il-Sung has been proclaimed chairman of the People's Republic of Korea at Seoul. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [3, 18, 22]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao15.xml", "Taiwan Strait - Nuclear Crisis", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. As one of the heroes of the PRC the High Command of the PLA has a new mission for you. The new North American government has retired the fleet that was guarding the Taiwan Strait. The wider stakes are clear: VICTORY Chiang Kai Shek has escaped from Taipei thanks to his American friends, but the whole Taiwanese island plus other minor islands are now part of the PRC. A strong result opens the road to Sino - Soviet Incident. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15, "support": [9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao16.xml", "Sino - Soviet Incident", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. 1-10-1955, Amur river, Sino-Soviet border, near Khabarovsk, Far Eastern Siberia. A chain of unfortunate incidents with the Soviets along the Chinese - Soviet border has opened the way for the outbreak of full scale military operations. The wider stakes are clear: I know you are the greatest hero of the PRC and the KRC and I have a mission for you from the Kremlin. A strong result opens the road to Great Leap Forward. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 89}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao17.xml", "Great Leap Forward", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Chinese revolution is surviving encirclement, invasion, and civil war. As our men from the KGB have told you, we are ready to support you, if you finally decide to undertake a coup against Mao Zedong and his reformed communism. We need to take China back to the right and true communist way. The wider stakes are clear: You are the new Premier of the People's Republic of China. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 233}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [89]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["The Great Patriotic War Russia Campaign (1942-1945)"],
["ruscam00.xml", "Operation Uranus", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. The time for retreating is over, now we must drive the fascist beasts from the soil of the Motherland! Now we began with Operation Uranus here on the Chir. The wider stakes are clear: The Soviet 21st Army and 5th Tank Army were able to capture some 27,000 Romanian prisoners—the bulk of three divisions— and then continue their advance southwards. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam01.xml", "Operation Saturn", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Now is the time to crush the Italians. General Fyodor Isidorovich Kuznetsov's 1st Guards Army and General Dmitri Danilovich Lelyushenko's 3rd Guards Army attacked from the north, encircling 130,000 soldiers of the Italian 8th Army on the Don and advancing to Millerovo. (Manstein sent the 6th Panzer Division to the Italians' aid of the 130,000 encircled troops, 45,000 survived to join the Panzers at Chertkovo on 17 January). Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{'country': 12, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam02.xml", "Magyar Massacre", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Clear the Highway of Hungarians and break their line of communications and reinforcement in support of our attack in the south on Rostov and Kharkov. On January 13, 1943, Russian forces, overwhelming in numbers and equipment, began the Voronezh-Kharkov Strategic Offensive Operation on the Bryansk, Voronezh, and Southwestern Fronts simultaneously. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 4, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam03.xml", " During Operation Star", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. We have swung you around to the north now, a little more now and we liberate Izium, we must drive on, drive the point of the sword through and gut the Fascist beast. As the German Sixth Army was encircled in Stalingrad, the Red Army undertook a series of wider offensives against the rest of Army Group South. The wider stakes are clear: These culminated on 2 January 1943, when the Soviets launched Operation Star, which between January and early February broke German defenses and led to the Soviet recapture of Kharkov, Belgorod and Kursk. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam04.xml", "Kursk", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Here at Prokhorovka you have been attached to the 5th Guards Tank Army, this will not be easy Comrade General. Directly facing you is the elite of the SS: Adolf Hitler's named Liebstandarte Division and Das Reich in the south. The wider stakes are clear: Regardless of the tactical outcome, the Battle of Prokhorovka was turned into a critical propaganda and operational victory for the Red Army. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam05.xml", "Orel Counter Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Here is our counter stroke to the German operations aimed at Kursk, it is to break through at Karachev and destroy this fortified salient around Orel. Beware the Fortresses at both Orel and Bryansk are fortified with heavy artillery, invest these fortresses and we shall move west. The wider stakes are clear: Operation Kutuzov set the stage for the liberation of Smolensk in September 1943. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam06.xml", "Krivoi Rog", "There is nowhere left to yield: hold this ground and make the enemy pay for every hex. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. On 17 October Konev attacked out of his bridgehead at Kremenchug and swung to the south toward the iron ore center at Krivoi Rog and the main rail line into the Dnepr bend from the west. This threat forced the Germans to give up Dnepropetrovsk, but the First Panzer Army was able to hold in front of Krivoi Rog. The wider stakes are clear: While the attack seemed of little value, it did force the Germans back, even further from the Dnepr and any territory freed, meant a better hope for life to the civilians there. Use terrain, entrenchment, and supporting fire to survive the first blow—then punish every exposed formation.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam07.xml", "Crossing Kiev", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Kiev has languished for too long under Nazi rule, they impatiently await your liberation. Nobody has said this will be easy, undoubtedly the Germans will throw much strength into the defence of the city in their fortress ideology. The wider stakes are clear: On the morning of 3 November 1943, the 4th Panzer Army awoke to a massive Soviet bombardment. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam08.xml", "Zhitomir Halt", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Taking Zhitomir will cut communications between Army Groups North and South, the 25th Panzer Division under General Jauer is counter-attacking here reinforced by Fallschirmjagers. The first unit to arrive from 48th Panzer Corps was the newly formed 25th Panzer Division commanded by General der Panzertruppen Georg Jauer, on 7 November. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam09.xml", "Iasi Invasion", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. STAVKA feels that the whole Romanian army here can be brought down with a few hard blows, your mission is to apply those blows here at Iasi. The First Jassy-Kishinev Offensive, was fought between 8 April and 6 June 1944 by the Soviets and Axis powers of World War II. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam10.xml", "Operation Bagration", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Three years ago, the fascists invaded Mother Russia causing untold suffering to the Russian people. Today on the 3rd anniversary of that hateful day, we begin the final Operation to drive them from our soil, Operation Bagration shall be their crescendo of doom. The wider stakes are clear: Bobruisk was liberated on June 29, the German 383rd Infantry Division commencing withdrawal towards dawn: no further elements of Ninth Army would escape from east of the Berezina. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam11.xml", "Minsk Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Here at Minsk the Germans have little chance of reinforcement before you surround them and destroy their Festung. With this action we will completely encircle their 4th Army from the north. The wider stakes are clear: In total, around 100,000 troops from Fourth and Ninth Armies were caught in the encirclement, of whom some 40,000 were killed, most of the remainder being captured. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam12.xml", "Vilnius Offensive", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Chernyakhovsky ordered that his main mobile 'exploitation' forces, the 5th Guards Tank Army and 3rd Guards Cavalry Corps continue their advance from Minsk on July 5 in the direction of Vilnius, with the aim of reaching the city by the following day: they were to encircle Vilnius from the south and north respectively. The rifle divisions of 5th Army were ordered to follow and close up to them. The wider stakes are clear: Without the traffic network based on Vilnius, the German position in the northern Baltics was untenable. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam13.xml", "The Gates of Warsaw", "The enemy has filled the approaches with strongpoints, but the city beyond them is the campaign's prize. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. After the Russian reconnaissance units reached Warsaw in late July, on August 1, 1944 the Warsaw Uprising started. Starting from an area south of Minsk Mazowiecki, Lieutenant-General N. D. Vedeneev's 3rd Tank Corps (part of the Soviet Second Tank Army) thrust northwest through Okuniew and Wolomin to Radzymin, reaching an area only three miles (five kilometers) from the strategic bridge over the Narew River at Zegrze. The wider stakes are clear: Between August 1 and August 10, 1944 at the conclusion of the Belorussian strategic offensive operation near the town of Radzymin in the vicinity of Warsaw, part of which entailed a large tank battle at Wolomin.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam14.xml", "Debrecen", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Cavalry-Mechanized Group Pliyev is in danger of being cut off at Nyiregyhaza, your Corps has been attached to the 6th Guards Tank Army and will attack north from Debrecen in order to relieve Cavalry Mechanized Group Pliyev. Holding Nyiregyhaza will cut off the escape route of the German 8th Army. The wider stakes are clear: The Debrecen operation saw Soviet forces advance anywhere from 60 to 120 miles further west into Hungary, leaving the 2nd and 3rd Ukrainian Fronts in position to renew the offensive towards Budapest. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam15.xml", "Budapest Offensive", "The enemy has filled the approaches with strongpoints, but the city beyond them is the campaign's prize. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. On 29 October 1944, the Red Army started its offensive against the city of Budapest. More than 1,000,000 men split into two operating maneuver groups rushed towards the city. The wider stakes are clear: While this destroyed most of the German forces in the region, troops were rushed from the Western Front and, in March, the Germans launched the ill fated Operation Spring Awakening (Unternehmen Fruhlingserwachen) in the Lake Balaton area. Use artillery and infantry together, isolate strongpoints, and avoid wasting elite units in unsupported assaults.", [{'country': 4, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam16.xml", "East Prussian Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. The main thrust of the offensive will be conducted by the 3rd Belorussian Front under Chernyakhovsky. Your forces are tasked with driving westwards towards Konigsberg, against the defensive positions of Third Panzer Army and Fourth Army, the northern armies of General Georg-Hans Reinhardt's Army Group Center. The wider stakes are clear: The last elements were cleared from Pillau on April 25 in the Zemland offensive operation. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam17.xml", "Stargard tank battle", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Operation Solstice (German: Unternehmen Sonnenwende), also known as Unternehmen Husarenritt or the 'Stargard tank battle', was a German armoured offensive operation on the Eastern Front, one of the last such operations. It was repulsed by the Red Army, but helped to convince the Soviet High Command to postpone the planned attack on Berlin. The wider stakes are clear: German forces failed to penetrate towards Kustrin and suffered major losses of heavy equipment in the subsequent retreat. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam18.xml", "Seelow Heights", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. In the early hours of 16 April, the offensive began with a massive bombardment by thousands of artillery pieces and Katyushas. Well before dawn, the 1st Belorussian Front attacked across the Oder and the 1st Ukrainian Front attacked across the Neisse. The wider stakes are clear: However, the Soviet forces led by Zhukov eventually broke through the defensive positions, having suffered about 30,000 casualties, while the Germans lost 12,000 personnel. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam19.xml", "The Last Battle: Berlin", "A city is not captured in a single blow; it is taken district by district under smoke and fire. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. On the walls of the houses we saw Goebbels' appeals, hurriedly scrawled in white paint: 'Every German will defend his capital. Steel pillboxes, barricades, mines, traps, suicide squads with grenades clutched in their hands all are swept aside before the tidal wave. The wider stakes are clear: At 02:41 on the morning of 7 May 1945, at the SHAEF headquarters, German Chief-of-Staff General Alfred Jodl signed the unconditional surrender documents for all German forces to the Allies. The city rewards combined arms and patience; reckless attacks will leave your best formations buried in rubble.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["Russian Counter-Offensive Campaign (1942-1946)"],
["rcampx01.xml", "Operation Uranus", "Stalingrad is burning, but the German Sixth Army has finally pushed itself into a trap. As Zhukov, coordinate the blow that will close Operation Uranus: smash the Axis flanks, cut the roads across the Don and Chir, and prevent relief forces from reopening the corridor to Paulus. The Romanian armies are brittle, yet German armour and air power can still punish a careless advance. Break through quickly, preserve your mobile formations for exploitation, and turn the defence of Stalingrad into the encirclement that changes the course of the war.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx02.xml", "Operation Saturn", "The Stalingrad pocket is sealed, but the wider Axis front on the Don has not yet collapsed. Italian formations, fortified western approaches, and a strongly defended central airfield block the next stage of the counteroffensive. Strike before the enemy can recover from Operation Uranus, destroy the Italian Eighth Army’s cohesion, and open the road toward Millerovo and Rostov. A rapid victory will expand the encirclement and deny Manstein the forces he needs for a relief attempt. Use armour for depth, not merely for the first line, and keep the winter advance moving.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx03.xml", "The Road to Rostov", "The Chir and Don crossings are heavily guarded, and German aircraft are already moving east to reinforce the threatened sector. Your task is to rupture the river line, seize the bridges, and create the deployment space required for the advance on Rostov. The enemy expects the rivers to slow you long enough for reserves to arrive; prove that expectation fatal. Concentrate artillery on a narrow front, force the crossings under cover, and exploit immediately with mobile units before the defensive network can be rebuilt.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx04.xml", "Airstrike Rostov", "Rostov is the gateway to the Caucasus, but the assault cannot begin until several tactical deployment sites are secured around the city. Reconnaissance reports limited defenders and little air cover—an opportunity that will vanish as soon as the enemy understands your intention. Advance with speed, seize the staging areas intact, and protect the corridors through which the main army must follow. This is a preparation battle in which every turn saved matters: the better your opening position, the less costly the coming struggle for Rostov will be.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx05.xml", "Rostov", "Rostov has been reinforced by the Wiking Panzer Division, including heavy Tigers, anti-tank batteries, cavalry, and local air support. The enemy intends to turn the city into a shield for the Caucasus withdrawal and a fortress on the Don. Use reconnaissance to identify the heavy armour, isolate the strongest positions, and attack the city from more than one direction. A frontal rush will burn away your tank strength; combined arms and careful encirclement can instead trap the defenders and open the southern road toward the Crimea.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx06.xml", "Sevastopol", "Sevastopol stands behind coastal guns, prepared urban defences, and incoming airborne reinforcements. Soviet marines, naval forces, aircraft, and paratroopers have already secured footholds around the fortress, but the final assault must be coordinated before Axis help arrives across the Black Sea. Suppress the batteries, protect the landing zones, and break into the city without allowing the defenders to concentrate against a single approach. The capture of Sevastopol will restore a vital base and place the entire Crimean coast within reach.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx07.xml", "Northwest to Odessa", "The road north from Sevastopol appears lightly held, but scattered Axis units and reconnaissance aircraft can still delay the movement toward Odessa. Treat these skirmishes as an operational race: clear the route, preserve fuel and ammunition, and prevent isolated enemy groups from cutting your columns or reporting their strength. Your army must arrive at the next battlefield organised rather than exhausted. A clean pursuit will keep the Black Sea initiative in Soviet hands and ensure that the heavy guns waiting farther west face a concentrated army, not a string of vulnerable detachments.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx08.xml", "Odessa", "Odessa is protected by dense anti-tank positions, heavy artillery, Italian naval elements, and two formidable railway guns. The enemy has prepared the coastal approaches to punish armour and delay any direct assault, but Soviet naval gunfire and bomber support are becoming available. Neutralise the long-range batteries, secure the shoreline, and open safe lanes for infantry and tanks to enter the city. This is a combined-arms siege: victory depends on using sea, air, artillery, and ground forces as a single system rather than feeding units into the fortifications piecemeal.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx09.xml", "German Counterattack Kharkov", "Kursk has been liberated, but German forces are regrouping around Kharkov under experienced commanders and have shot down the aircraft sent to examine their positions. You must advance with incomplete intelligence against a city that has changed hands before and will be defended by armour, artillery, and mobile reserves. Probe carefully, secure the approaches, and avoid exposing your spearheads to a prepared counterstroke. Take Kharkov, break the enemy’s ability to stabilise the front, and clear the way toward the Dnieper operations that will follow.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx10.xml", "To Kiev - But First Kanev", "German and Romanian remnants are holding Kanev to protect the approaches to Kiev and the Dnieper crossings. The visible garrison appears small, but Luftwaffe activity has blinded reconnaissance along the river and hidden whatever reserves wait beyond the city limits. Seize the crossings, eliminate the holdouts, and establish a secure bridgehead before the main battle for Kiev begins. Speed is important, but a careless river assault could leave your formations divided on opposite banks. Take Kanev cleanly and give the armies converging on Kiev a firm southern anchor.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx11.xml", "Kiev", "The battle for Kiev is already under way. Konev, Malinovsky, and Vatutin are attacking from the north and centre while your force approaches from the south through uncertain terrain and hostile air cover. Your role is to reinforce the encirclement, seize the southern crossings, and prevent the garrison from escaping or receiving relief. Kiev is too large for a single thrust: isolate districts, coordinate armour with infantry, and keep supply routes across the river open. Liberate the city without allowing the battle to consume the army needed for the advance beyond Ukraine.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx12.xml", "Belgrade Liberation", "With Kiev secured, Romanian resistance around Belgrade threatens the flank and communications of the wider Soviet advance. Enemy tanks, anti-tank guns, and mixed Axis units defend the approaches, while damaged airfields must be captured before your own aviation can operate effectively. Clear the region, seize the bases, and eliminate the possibility of a counterattack from the south. This operation is less spectacular than Berlin, but strategically essential: leave an enemy force behind you and every supply column moving toward Poland will remain in danger.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx13.xml", "Poland", "The armies driving through Poland are waiting for your formation on the south-eastern sector of the front. Luftwaffe patrols have destroyed reconnaissance aircraft, but airborne reinforcements are prepared to seize advanced positions and accelerate the junction. Break through the remaining German screen, protect the drop zones, and connect your force with the neighbouring Soviet armies before the enemy can defeat either element separately. Success will complete the concentration for the final advance to the Oder; delay will give Berlin precious time to fortify its approaches.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx14.xml", "The Road to Berlin", "The Oder line is the last great operational barrier before Berlin. Enemy troops are scattered around the approaches, city limits are heavily armed, and surprise detachments wait beyond the areas visible to reconnaissance. Secure the crossings, destroy isolated strongpoints, and bring your army into position before the Western Allies can reach the German capital first. The defenders are depleted but still dangerous, especially where anti-tank guns and urban terrain can halt Soviet armour. Open the road to Berlin and preserve enough strength for the battles inside the city.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx15.xml", "The Battle of Berlin", "Berlin is surrounded, but the Luftwaffe and dense anti-aircraft defences have forced Soviet reconnaissance out of the city. The enemy has converted streets, rail yards, government buildings, and hidden arsenals into a layered defensive system whose true strength remains uncertain. Drive into the capital, divide the garrison, and seize the crossings before the defenders can shift reserves between sectors. Expect ambushes, heavy anti-tank fire, and close urban combat. This is not yet the Reichstag assault—it is the battle to make that final objective reachable.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx16.xml", "The Fall of the Reichstag", "The Reichstag has become the last symbol and one of the strongest fortresses in Berlin. Its defenders possess more ammunition, anti-tank weapons, and heavy artillery than intelligence predicted, while barricades and firing positions have appeared overnight. Reduce the surrounding blocks, isolate the building, and bring infantry and engineers forward under concentrated fire support. Do not squander tanks against hidden guns in the streets. Take the Reichstag, raise the red banner over the centre of German power, and end the European war with a victory worthy of the losses that brought you here.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx17.xml", "Berlin Standoff", "The guns have barely fallen silent when the alliance begins to fracture. Soviet engineers fortify the eastern sector of Berlin while American, British, and French troops face them across a tense line of demarcation. Orders are to hold ground and avoid opening fire—but an unexpected Allied attack turns occupation into a new battlefield. Stabilise the sector, protect the approaches to East Berlin, and decide whether this clash remains local or becomes the opening shot of another war. Every unit lost now will matter if negotiations fail completely.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx18.xml", "Conquer Europe?", "Victory over Germany has produced an impossible choice. In this alternate path, Soviet leaders form a new Pact of Steel with former German enemies and Italian forces in order to drive the Western Allies from Europe. British, American, and French armies are retreating toward Dunkirk while German formations secure the northern flank. Commit to the offensive, reorganise a coalition built from yesterday’s enemies, and strike before the evacuation ports can be fortified. The decision taken here abandons historical restraint and opens a campaign of continental conquest.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx19.xml", "Taking of Dunkirk", "The Western Allies are compressed around Dunkirk, but the port remains their gateway to the English Channel. Soviet, German, and Italian forces must break the siege perimeter, seize an airfield and deployment zone, and prevent another evacuation across the water. Naval and air support are available, yet transport capacity is limited and heavy artillery cannot all be moved forward at once. Secure the coast, destroy the remaining bridgehead, and establish the bases required for an invasion of Britain. Failure here will give the Allies time to rebuild behind the Channel.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx20.xml", "English Channel", "Operation Nexus carries the new coalition across the English Channel. British, American, and French forces contest the crossing while Soviet and allied transports struggle to deliver armour, artillery, and paratroopers to the southern coast. Capture an airfield immediately or enemy aircraft will turn the beaches and sea lanes into a graveyard. Then seize the deployment zone, widen the lodgement, and prevent the defenders from containing the invasion. The operation is a race between reinforcement and destruction: establish a functioning bridgehead before the Channel closes behind you.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx21.xml", "Annexation of South England", "The invasion has gained a foothold in southern England, and allied armies are pushing toward London from the north. Your force must annex the southern approaches, secure roads and airbases, and prepare the advance on Windsor. The countryside may appear open, but British reserves can use towns, rivers, and narrow routes to delay heavier formations. Keep the landing areas supplied, prevent local counterattacks from reaching the coast, and build a continuous front. A swift southern advance will close the first half of the ring around the British capital.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx22.xml", "Windsor 1946", "Windsor is heavily fortified and stands between your southern army and the encirclement of London. German units have reached the north-eastern outskirts while paratroopers and advance detachments hold scattered tactical positions inside the metropolitan area. Exploit identified gaps, secure the airborne landing zones, and break the Windsor defences before British reserves can seal the corridor. The city’s air and ground support remains strong, so every isolated spearhead risks destruction. Take Windsor, connect the encircling forces, and prepare for the final struggle for London.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx23.xml", "London Blitz", "Britain and France have capitulated, and the war crosses the Atlantic. A Soviet-German naval force, supported by submarines, destroyers, aircraft, and landing troops, approaches the Florida coast before American radar detects the deployment. Enemy destroyers and air units guard the objective, but no reinforcements are expected during the opening assault. Win control of the sea, suppress the coastal defence, and seize the first strategic point intact. This is the campaign’s most audacious leap: if the lodgement fails, the ocean will separate the invaders from every source of heavy reinforcement.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx24.xml", "Onward to the USA", "The first American coastal position lies east of Florida, while other coalition armies strike farther north. Your air support will remain limited until an airbase is captured, leaving ships and landing forces exposed during the opening turns. Secure the tactical point, take the airfield, and expand the beachhead before American forces can coordinate a counterattack. Naval gunfire can open the way, but only ground units can hold what has been won. Establish the bridgehead that will carry the war from the Atlantic shore into the American interior.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx25.xml", "Florida Landing", "The Florida landing has succeeded, and the invasion front is moving north. Savannah is strongly fortified, but a captured airbase gives your army access to air and naval support while reinforcements approach from the coast. The city anchors the American southern defence and blocks the route toward Washington. Isolate its fortifications, protect the supply corridor to the beaches, and coordinate bombardment with a deliberate ground assault. Take Savannah before the defenders can turn it into a prolonged siege and allow the northern coalition armies to join the advance inland.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx26.xml", "Red Savannah", "Savannah has fallen and the road toward the American capital is opening. Coalition armies are driving south and west from the Atlantic while your force prepares the next stage of the offensive. American resistance is reorganising around key transport routes, industrial centres, and the approaches to Washington. Keep the columns moving, capture airfields and supply hubs, and prevent the defenders from forming a continuous line. This is the final operational advance of the campaign: every intact unit and every turn saved will strengthen the assault on the capital.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx27.xml", "Washington in Flames", "Washington is the final objective of the impossible war that began at Stalingrad and crossed two oceans. The American capital is defended by surviving regular forces, emergency formations, artillery, and whatever air support can still be assembled. Break the outer defensive ring, secure the Potomac crossings, and fight through the government district without allowing your supply line to collapse behind you. The battle is both military and symbolic: victory ends organised resistance and completes the alternate-history conquest. Commit every veteran formation carefully—there will be no campaign beyond Washington in which to replace them.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["Standalone Historical Battles"],
["1920_perekop.xml", "1920 Siege of Perekop", "1920 Siege of Perekop<br>\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af<br>Comrade General, we are now in the position to attack the Isthmus of Perekop and northern Crimea, where Wrangel's White Army has entrenched themselves. Prepare for long and hard fighting! You will also command Makhno's Black Army in this operation.<br><br>Scenario Version: January 2021<br>Scenario Type: Historic<br>Player Countries: Red Russia, Black Army<br>AI Version: 3.0<br>Player Turn Prestige 20pp/turn<br>Turns: 16 BV; 20 V; 26 TV<br>Scenario Designer: randowe<br><br>ORDERS:<br>\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af<br>Break through the enemy defensive lines and attack the Isthmus of Perekop as well as northern Crimea and capture all VHs in 16/20/26 turns for a Brilliant Victory/Victory/Tactical Victory.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103, "support": [136]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-atomic"],
]
